hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"12025","(12025) Sharik told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, that Omar prayed over bones in the Levant."
"12026","(12026) Marwan narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi. He was asked about a dead man who was found with three parts of his head cut off. In a neighborhood, and his middle is in a neighborhood and his feet are in a neighborhood, he said, he prays on the middle."
"12027","(12027) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aamir bin Rabi’ah, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was informed of this. He said: When you see the funeral procession, stand for it until it leaves you, or is placed. (Bukhari 1307, Abu Dawud 3164)"
"12028","(12028) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Ubad Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Amir bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, such as the hadith of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, or something similar. (Bukhari 1308, Muslim 75)"
"12029","(12029) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Pass by The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed his funeral, so he stood up and said to those with him, “Get up, for death has a fear.” (Ibn Majah 1543. Ahmad 2/287)"
"12030","(12030) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Othman bin Hakim narrated to us: On the authority of Kharijiyah bin Zayd, on the authority of his uncle Yazid. Ibn Thabit, that he was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, among his companions, and a funeral procession appeared, and when the Messenger of God saw it May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he revolted and his companions revolted, and they did not stop standing until it crossed, and God does not know who was harmed by it, or Because of the narrowness of the place, I did not consider it to be anything but Judaism, or a Jew, and We did not ask it about its resurrection. (Ahmad 4/388, Hakim 591)"
"12031","(12031) Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Muammar Abdullah bin Sakhbari, that Abu Musa He told them that whenever a funeral procession passed by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he would stand up until it passed it. (Abu Ali 266)"
"12032","(12032) Al-Fadl and Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawwi, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Saeed said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you see the funeral procession, get up."
"12033","(12033) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, that a funeral passed by him and he got up and said: Marwan told him: Sit down, and he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a funeral procession passed by him and he stood up, so Marwan stood up.

(Nasa’i 2046. Ahmad 3/53)"
"12034","(12034) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, that Qais and Abu Masoud passed With his funeral, they stood up."
"12035","(12035) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, who said: They said to Ali: Indeed, Abu Musa ordered Thus, he said: The angels will be with her, so stand up for her."
"12036","(12036) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: I did not know anyone who would stand up when they passed by. Who is responsible for the funeral procession other than Amr bin Maymun?"
"12037","(12037) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, that he and Salem ibn Abdullah witnessed it. A funeral procession passed by them, and Salem stood up, but Saeed did not."
"12038","(12038) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Al-Muhajir, who said: I saw Al-Sha’bi. A funeral procession passed by him and he got up."
"12039","(12039) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: Al-Hasan bin Ali was sitting and he passed by him. A funeral. The people stood up when the funeral took place and said: Al-Hasan bin Ali just passed by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to conduct his funeral. A Jew, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sitting on his way, and he thought that his funeral should rise above his head. A Jew, so he stood up. (Nasa’i 2054, Ahmad 1/201)"
"12040","(12040) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, that Qays ibn Sa’d and Sahl Ibn Hanif were in Al-Qadisiyah, when a funeral passed by them and they got up, and it was said to them: She is from the people of the earth, so they said: Indeed, the Messenger A funeral procession passed by him, and he stood up and was told that he was a Jew, so he said: Isn’t she a soul? (Bukhari 1312, Muslim 661)"
"12041","(12041) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Ali, he said We were sitting, and a funeral passed by, so we stood up. He said: What is this? We said: This is the command of Abu Musa. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, only stood up. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him once, then he did not return. (Ahmad 142. An-Nasa’i 2050)"
"12042","(12042) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said: We were with Ali and he passed by. Ali was having his funeral, then a man stood up and Ali said: What is this? It is as if this is the work of the Jews."
"12043","(12043) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of al-Hasan ibn Ali and Ibn Abbas that they saw a funeral. So one of them stood up and the other sat down, and the one who stood up said to the one who did not stand up: Did not the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stand up? He said: Yes, then he sat down. (Nasa’i 2052. Tabarani 2747)"
"12044","(12044) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: The companions of Ali and the companions of Abdullah were not They stand up for funerals when they pass by."
"12045","(12045) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The companions of Abdullah had dates There are funerals, but not one of them will get up."
"12046","(12046) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They did not stand up for funerals when they passed by."
"12047","(12047) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Laith, who said: There was Ata and Mujahid who saw the funeral, but neither of them stood up. To her."
"12048","(12048) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Masoud ibn al-Hakam, he said: He said: Ali rose The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to the funeral, so we stood up, then he sat down, and we sat down. (Abu Dawud 3167. Tirmidhi 1044)"
"12049","(12049) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Artaah bin Al-Mundhir, that Abu Al-Darda’ was a Jewish neighbor of his."
"12050","(12050) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Yahya bin Amari, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: Abu Talib fell ill and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited him. (Tirmidhi 3232, Hakim 432)"
"12051","(12051) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Isa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jubayr, on the authority of Anas, who said: He was a young man. A Jew serving the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he fell ill, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to him to visit him."
"12052","(12052) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Abbad told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: that Abu Talib He fell ill and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recovered him."
"12053","(12053) Hushaym and Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. May peace and blessings be upon him on his grave after he was buried. (Bukhari 1319. Abu Dawud 53)"
"12054","(12054) Hushaym told us, he said: Othman bin Hakim informed us, Kharijiyah bin Zaid informed us, on the authority of his uncle Yazid. Ibn Thabit, who was older than Zaid, said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when we reached Al-Baqi’, we found With a new grave, he asked about it, and they said: This is so-and-so. He recognized her, so he came to the grave and we lined up behind him, so he said the takbir over her four times."
"12055","(12055) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Hamid Ibn Hilal, that Al-Bara’ Ibn Ma’rur died before The arrival of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Medina. When he arrived, he prayed upon him."
"12056","(12056) Yahya bin Adam told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed over the dead after he was buried. (Abu Ali 2517)"
"12057","(12057) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, that the mother of Sa’d ibn His servant died while he was absent, so when he came, he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I would love for you to pray. Ali Umm Saad, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to her grave and prayed over her. (Tirmidhi 1038, Bayhaqi 48)"
"12058","(12058) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Qasim: That the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to Al-Baqi’. He saw a new grave, and said: What is this grave? It was said: So-and-so was the master of Banu Ghanam, which used to maintain the mosque, so he prayed over her.

(Abdul Razzaq 6541)"
"12059","(12059) Hushaym narrated to us, Ash’ath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Qarza bin Ka’b came in a group with him, and he Ali Ibn Hanif prayed for him and he was buried, so Ali ordered him and his companions to pray over the grave, so he did so."
"12060","(12060) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Salman bin Rabi’ah came and Abdullah had prayed. Ali's funeral, and Abdullah said to him: Go forward and pray for your brother with your companions."
"12061","(12061) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Aban Al-Attar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir that he was informed that Anas prayed over his funeral after he had prayed over her."
"12062","(12062) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulkiya, he said: Abd al-Rahman Ibn Abi died. A virgin in a house where he was, so We carried him on our necks six miles to Mecca while Aisha was absent, so she came back after So, she said, “Show me his grave,” so they showed her and she prayed over him."
"12063","(12063) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Asim ibn Umar died, and Ibn Umar was absent and came back after That, Ayoub said, “I think it is.” He said, “Three.” He said, “Show me my brother’s grave, so show him the funeral prayer over him.”"
"12064","(12064) Hushaym told us, Abu Hurriya told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he used to say that if a man precedes the funeral Let him pray over the grave."
"12065","(12065) Hushaym told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, he said: I was with Ibn Sirin and we wanted a funeral. So we preceded her until she was buried. He said: Then Ibn Sirin said: Come, so that we may do as they did. He said: So he said the takbir over the grave four times."
"12066","(12066) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, a partner narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Muradi, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Khaythama, that Abu Musa prayed for Al-Harith bin Qais after he had prayed for him. He brought them to a coward, so he prayed. After he prayed upon him, Yahya said: And a bitter partner said: Abu Musa prayed for him and asked forgiveness for him."
"12067","(12067) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Muthanna bin Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, that Bashir bin Ka’b ended up at a funeral. He prayed for her and prayed for her."
"12068","(12068) Saeed bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl, on the authority of His father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to visit the poor people of Medina, and he would attend their funerals when They died. He said: Then a woman from the family of Al-Awali died, so we buried her. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked to He buried her, prayed the funeral prayer for her and said “Allahu Akbar” four times."
"12069","(12069) Dawud bin Abdullah narrated to us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zaid bin Al-Muhajir bin Qunfud, On the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by the grave of a hadith, and said: What is this grave? They said: The grave of so-and-so. He said: Why do you not permit me? So he stood in line and he prayed. (Ibn Majah 1529. Ahmad 3/444)"
"12070","(12070) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The funeral prayer is not performed twice over the dead."
"12071","(12071) Hushaym told us, saying: Abu Hurr told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that when he preceded the funeral, he would ask forgiveness No and he sits, or leaves."
"12072","(12072) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: Al-Hasan did not think that he should pray over the grave."
"12073","(12073) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Abu al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: A brother of yours has died, so get up and pray over him, meaning Negus (Tirmidhi 1039. Muslim 67)"
"12074","(12074) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Your brother, the Negus, has died, so pray for him. (Ahmad 4/441)"
"12075","(12075) Affan narrated to us, Bishr bin Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similar to the hadith of Abdul-Ala. (Tirmidhi 1039. An-Nasa’i 2102)"
"12076","(12076) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hamran bin Anas, on the authority of Abu al-Tufayl, on the authority of Ibn Jariyah Al-Ansari, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Your brother the Negus has died, so pray for him.

(Ibn Majah 1536. Ahmad 4/64)"
"12077","(12077) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Al-Najashi had died, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to Al-Baqi’ and his companions, so we lined up behind him and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, advanced. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said “Allahu Akbar” four times."
"12078","(12078) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jarir, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Your brother, the Negus, has died, so ask forgiveness for him.

(Ahmad 4/363, Tabarani 2347)"
"12079","(12079) Zayd bin Harun told us, Sulaym bin Hayyan told us, Saeed bin Mina told us, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed for Asahmah the Negus and said the “Allahu Akbar” over him four times."
"12080","(12080) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin: That the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed for the Negus. Al-Hasan said, “He only prayed for him.”"
"12081","(12081) Muammar bin Sulaiman Al-Ruqi told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; A man has more right to wash his wife and pray for her."
"12082","(12082) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that if he preceded the funeral, the father had more right. By praying over the woman, then the husband, then the brother."
"12083","(12083) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A man has more right to his wife even if he marries her."
"12084","(12084) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Sulayman, on the authority of Masruq, who said: A woman died for Umar. He said: I had more right to her when she was alive, but now you have more right to her."
"12085","(12085) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad which of them is more worthy of praying over a woman, and Al-Hakam said: The brother, and Hammad said: Ibrahim said: The imam, and if they take turns, then the guardian, then the husband."
"12086","(12086) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If the woman dies, their bond between them is cut off. And between her two wives."
"12087","(12087) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The father, the son, and the brother are more worthy of blessings upon the woman than The husband"
"12088","(12088) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his followers, that he used to say: The saints are more deserving of prayer. Aliyah from the husband."
"12089","(12089) Ibn Abi Ghani told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: If the woman dies, the relationship between them is cut off. And between her husband and her guardians, she has more right to her."
"12090","(12090) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qays, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The husband is more worthy than the brother."
"12091","(12091) Shababi told us, Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Abu Ka’b, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abi Bakra, he said: She was a woman from Banu Tamim, the wife of Abu Bakra, and she died, and they disputed over the prayer over her, so he prayed over her. Abu Bakra, and he said: If I had not been the most deserving of you to pray for her, I would not have prayed for her."
"12092","(12092) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, who said: The funeral prayer was not performed upon Abu Bakr except in the mosque."
"12093","(12093) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir ibn Zayd, on the authority of al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, he said: May the blessings of God be upon my father. Bakr and Omar facing the pulpit."
"12094","(12094) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that Umar prayed for him in The mosque"
"12095","(12095) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, Fulayh bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Salih bin Al-Ajlan, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubair: On the authority of Aisha, who said: By God, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not pray for Suhail Ibn Bayda except In the mosque. (Muslim 1000, Tirmidhi 1033)"
"12096","(12096) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, our sheikhs narrated to us, that Omar prayed upon him at the pulpit, and he made People pray for him in crowds."
"12097","(12097) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Salih, the guardian of the twins, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever prays at a funeral in the mosque has no prayer for him. He said: They were the companions of the Messenger of God. If the place becomes too tight for them, may God bless him and grant him peace, they return and do not pray. (Abu Dawud 3184; Ibn Majah 1517)"
"12098","(12098) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Salih, the guardian of the twins, on the authority of the one who caught up with Abu Bakr and Omar. When the prayer became too crowded, they would leave and would not pray at the funeral in the mosque."
"12099","(12099) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ayman, on the authority of Kathir bin Abbas, who said: No. Do you know that you prayed over a funeral in the mosque?"
"12100","Abu Abdul Rahman Buqiy bin Mukhlid told us, Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shayba told us.

(12100) Salam Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, he said: Ali was When he comes to the man’s obituary, he says: To Allah we belong and to Him we shall return, O Allah, raise his rank among the righteous, And leave him behind among those who left behind, and we seek him with You, Lord of the worlds. Do not lead us astray after him, and do not deprive us of his reward."
"12101","(12101) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, Abu Misra told us: When He came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to kill Zayd and Ja’far, and Abdullah Ibn Rawahih mentioned their matter, so he said: Oh God. Forgive Zayd. O Allah, forgive Zayd. O Allah, forgive Zayd. O Allah, forgive Ja`far and Abdullah bin Rawahiyah. (Ibn Saad 46)"
"12102","(12102) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Harith bin Dhahir, he said: When Abdullah was reported to Abu Darda’, he said: He did not leave behind anyone like him."
"12103","(12103) Muhammad bin Fudail told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I informed Al-Hasan of the death of Al-Sha’bi, and he said: May God have mercy on him, and may God have mercy on him if he From Islam to a place."
"12104","(12104) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abjar, he said: I informed Al-Shu’abi of the death of Ibrahim, and he said: May God have mercy on him. He did not leave behind a successor like him, but if he was dead he was more knowledgeable than he was alive."
"12105","(12105) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, who said: They passed by my father’s funeral. Abdul Rahman Ali Abi Juhayfah, he said: He rested, and he was relieved from it."
"12106","(12106) Abu Asama told us, Shuabi told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: I came to Omar with my obituary. Al-Numan bin Muqrin said: He put his hand on his head and started crying."
"12107","(12107) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar was in the market and Wael ibn was mourned for him. A stone released its pills, and got up and was overcome by wailing."
"12108","(12108) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim ibn Abi Hafsa, on the authority of a man called Abu Kulthum, who said: I heard Ibn al-Hanafiyyah says at the funeral of Ibn Abbas, “Today the Lord of knowledge died.” (Hakim 535)"
"12109","(12109) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ammar, a client of Banu Hashim, who said: We sat in the shade of the palace with Ibn Abbas at the funeral of Zayd bin Thabit, and he said: Today a lot of knowledge has been buried."
"12110","(12110) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Alaqiyya, on the authority of al-Mughirah ibn Shu`bi: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade cursing the dead. (Tirmidhi 1982. Ahmad 4/252)"
"12111","(12111) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, the client of Banu Tha’labiya, on the authority of Qutba ibn Malik, who said: One of the princes insulted Ali, so Zaid bin Arqam stood up to him and said: As for me, I learned that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He forbade cursing the dead, so why did you curse Ali when he was dead? (Ahmad 4/369, Tabarani 4974)"
"12112","(12112) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, who said: I heard Hilal ibn Yassaf narrating on the authority of Amr ibn Al-Khattab, he delivered a sermon with manna on a mountain, and he said: Do not curse the dead, for whatever the dead curses the living will harm."
"12113","(12113) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiyah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: He curses the dead. Like one who oversees destruction."
"12114","(12114) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour ibn Safiyya, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Do not mention Your dead are only good."
"12115","(12115) Shababah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: The harm of a believer in His death is like his harm in his life."
"12116","(12116) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam ibn Yahya, on the authority of his followers, who said: I attended a funeral procession wearing bracelets, and they crowded together. At the funeral, Abu Al-Sawwar Al-Adawi said: You see, these are the best or companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. One of them was If he sees a load, he will carry it; otherwise, he will isolate himself, and will not harm anyone."
"12117","(12117) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mahdi, on the authority of a man called Ismail al-Jahdari, who said: We went out for a funeral. Al-Hasan witnessed it. He said: He saw a people crowding on the bed, so Al-Hasan said: What is the matter with these people? I think that Satan has sensed who people, so he followed them in order to reduce their wages."
"12118","(12118) Hushaym bin Bashir narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz bin Suhayb al-Bunani narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He said: His funeral passed. By the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he praised her so well that tongues followed one another, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: It is obligatory. He said: A funeral procession passed by him and he praised it so badly that tongues continued, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: It is obligatory, and he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab, O Messenger of God, you said in the first funeral, where she was praised well. It is obligatory, and you said likewise in the second, and he said: You are God’s witnesses on earth two or three times."
"12119","(12119) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Iyas ibn Salamah, on the authority of his father, he said: Pass by The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, attended the funeral of a man from the Ansar, and he praised it well, and said: It is obligatory, then he passed by it. With another funeral, it was praised other than that, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is obligatory. They said: O Messenger God and what it has imposed. He said: The angels are God’s witnesses in the heavens, and you are God’s witnesses on earth. (Tabarani 6262)"
"12120","(12120) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Pass by The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed his funeral and praised her with good deeds, and said: It is obligatory. Then they passed. In other words, he praised her evilly in the manner of evil, and said: It is certain that you are God’s witnesses on earth. (Ahmad 2/261, Abu Ali 5979)"
"12121","(12121) Affan narrated to us, Dawud bin Abi Al-Furat narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraydah, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad Al-Dilili, He said: I came to Medina and an illness had struck it, so I sat with Omar ibn Al-Khattab, and a funeral procession passed by them, and its companion praised it. Good, so Omar said: It is obligatory, then he passed by another and praised it badly, so Omar said: It is obligatory, so Abu Al-Aswad said: So I said, and what? Is it obligatory, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: I said, as the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever is a Muslim and has four witnesses will be well, God will admit him. Paradise, so we said, “And three?” He said: And three, so we said, and two. He said, and two, then we did not ask him about one. Bukhari 1368. Tirmidhi 1059"
"12122","(12122) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Khaythami, who said: Abdullah said: Look at the people when... Their beds, so if you see the servant dying in the best way you see him, then hope for the best for him, and if you see him dying in the best way you see him, then hope for the best for him. The evil of what you see, so fear for it."
"12123","(12123) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim bin Amir bin Masoud narrated to me, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A man died, and he was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet, and a good man praised him, so he said: It is due, and another died. An evil was mentioned about it, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said, “It is obligatory,” and some of the people said: It is strange what the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said. It was obligatory, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Some are witnesses against others."
"12124","(12124) Zaid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Who Whoever washes a dead person, let him wash himself, and whoever carries a funeral, let him perform ablution."
"12125","(12125) Shababi told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Salih, the client of the twins, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: Whoever washes a dead person, let him wash himself, and whoever carries him, let him perform ablution."
"12126","(12126) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Uthman, who said: Whoever carries my funeral, let him perform ablution."
"12127","(12127) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Urwah, who said: Whenever Ibn al-Zubair died, he would have a dead member of his family. He said: Hurry, hurry, go out, go out. He said: So he will come out in whatever hour it was."
"12128","(12128) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Abu Bakr died. On the Tuesday night, he was buried on the Tuesday night."
"12129","(12129) Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of al-Sha’abi, who said: It was said that when the Hour approached, death Suddenly"
"12130","(12130) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Adiy, on the authority of some of Abdullah’s companions, on the authority of Abdul God said: Sudden death is a relief to the believers and a hardship to the disbeliever."
"12131","(12131) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Malik bin Mughul narrated to us, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Tamim bin Salamah, he said: A man among us died. Suddenly, a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “He became angry, so I mentioned it to Abraham, and we were rarely We mentioned a hadith to Abraham, except that we found him with it, and he said: They hated it, and they seized it as grief seized it."
"12132","(12132) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abd God and Aisha said: Sudden death is compassionate to the believer and sorry to the ungodly."
"12133","(12133) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: I heard Mujahid bin Abi Rashid, saying: Mujahid said: One of the signs of the Hour is death. Home"
"12134","(12134) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated sudden death."
"12135","(12135) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Tamim bin Salamah, on the authority of Ubaid bin Khalid, a man from Companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding his sudden death, he said, “He was overcome with regret.” (Tirmidhi 982. Ahmad 3/424)"
"12136","(12136) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, who said: They were with a man from Abdullah’s companions. And he was sick, and he sweated on his forehead, so a man went and wiped the sweat from his forehead, and he hit his hand. Sufyan said: They are They used to prefer sweating for the dead."
"12137","(12137) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, that a friend of his from the marshes entered upon him. He returned, so he wiped his forehead and found him laughing, so some of the people said to him: What makes you laugh, Abu Shibl? He said: I laughed at Abdullah’s statement: The believer’s soul comes out cold, and if he has done evil, he will be hardened for it. upon death to be there, and the soul of the disbeliever or the immoral person comes out of his mouth just as the soul of a donkey comes out of it, and it is He has done good deeds, so it will be easy for him when he dies so that he can do so."
"12138","(12138) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The fur and socks should be removed from the dead person. And the two socks and the African socks, unless the socks complete a string, in which case they are left on, and he is buried with his clothes."
"12139","(12139) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: No sandals or shoes should be buried with the dead person."
"12140","(12140) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Al-Izar bin Harith Al-Abdi, who said: Zayd bin Suhan said: Do not remove any clothing from me except the socks, for I am a pilgrim. I will pilgrimage to you."
"12141","(12141) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, came with a funeral procession to pray over it. He said: Is he in debt? They said: Yes, two dinars. He said: Did he leave something for them? They said: No. He said: So pray for your companion. Abu Qatada said: What is upon me, O Messenger of God? So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Tirmidhi 1069, Darami 2593)"
"12142","(12142) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Iyas ibn Salamah, on the authority of his father: that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He came to the funeral of a man from the Ansar to pray for him, and he said: Did he leave anything behind? They said: No. He said: Is he in debt? They said: Yes, he has two dinars. He said: Pray for your friend. Abu Qatada said: They are upon me, O Messenger of God. He said: So he prayed. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Then Iyas told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was... Abu Qatada met him and said: What did the two dinars do? Even their judgement. (Bukhari 2289. Ahmad 4/47)"
"12143","(12143) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, He said: A man died, and we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to pray for him. He took a step, and said: Is he in debt? We said: Yes, two dinars. He said: Pray for your companion. (Ahmad 3/330, Bayhaqi 75)"
"12144","(12144) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Katheer, the servant of Laythiyan, narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abdullah bin Jahsh: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, what is the matter with you if you are killed? For the sake of God. He said: The jinn. Then when he turned away, he said: Except for the debt that Gabriel had shared with me just before. (Ahmad 4/350, Tabarani 557)"
"12145","(12145) Zaid bin Harun told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a similar manner, except that he said: He said to him Gabriel, peace be upon him. (Muslim 117 Tirmidhi 1712)"
"12146","(12146) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, Fudayl bin Ghazwan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought to the funeral of a man from the Ansar and he prayed over him, then said: What did he leave behind? They said: He left two dinars, or three. He said: He left two dinars, or three dinars. (Ahmad 2/429, Bazzar 3449)"
"12147","(12147) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Addah, he said: I heard Abu Imamah narrating On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, regarding a man who died and left behind a dinar or two dinars, he said: One or two dinars. (Ahmad 5/252, Tabarani 8008)"
"12148","(12148) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: He followed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. A black slave died, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought him and said: Look, did he leave anything behind? They said: He left behind two dinars. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Two dinars. (Ahmad 1/4051 Abu Ali 5015)"
"12149","(12149) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, Ja’far bin Sulaiman narrated to us, Utaiba narrated to us, on the authority of Burayd bin Asram, he said: I heard Ali says: A man from the people of Suffa died, and they said: O Messenger of God, he left behind a dinar and a dirham, and he said: two coins, so he said: Bless your companion. (Bukhari 1974)"
"12150","(12150) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I entered upon her. A Jew, so he gave her perfume, and said: May God protect you from the torment of the grave. She said: So I became distressed by that. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, I said: O Messenger of God, is there a torment in the grave? He said: Yes, they will be tortured in their graves with a punishment that animals can hear. (Bukhari 6366. Muslim 125)"
"12151","(12151) Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, according to the hadith of Abu Muawiyah."
"12152","(12152) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: seek refuge in God from hell, seek refuge in God from the torment of the grave, seek refuge in God from the temptations of Antichrist, seek refuge in God from the temptations of life and death. (Tirmidhi 3604)"
"12153","(12153) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nazra, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: Zaid bin narrated to us Thabit, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said, “This nation will be tested in its graves. If you had not buried it, I would have prayed.” May God make you hear from the torment of the grave from which I hear. Then he turned to us and said: Seek refuge in God from The torment of the grave. We said, “We seek refuge in God from the torment of the grave.” (Muslim 67 Ahmad 5/190)"
"12154","(12154) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Abdullah Al-Shakuri, on the authority of Al-Ma'roor bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The mother of my beloved, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, O God, grant me By my husband, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and by my father Abu Sufyan, and by my brother Muawiyah. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Indeed, you have asked God for specified terms, numbered days, and allotted provisions. He will not hasten anything before Its solution or delays something from its solution, even if you had asked God to protect you from torment in the Fire, or torment in the grave. It was better and better. (Muslim 2050, Ahmad 1/390)"
"12155","(12155) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Uthman al-Shahham, on the authority of Muslim ibn Abi Bakra, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to supplicate after the prayer, saying: O God, I seek refuge in You from disbelief, poverty, and the torment of the grave. (Ahmad 5/36. Tirmidhi 3503)"
"12156","(12156) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, on the authority of Omar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to seek refuge in God from cowardice, miserliness, the torment of the grave, and temptations of the chest. (Ahmad 1/22, Bazzar 324)"
"12157","(12157) Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Zazan: on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: We went out with The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was at the funeral of a man from the Ansar. So we went to the grave, and when he was dead, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat down. peace be upon him, and we sat around him, as if there were birds over our heads, and in his hand was a stick with which to scratch the ground, so he raised His head, and he said: Seek refuge in God from the torment of the grave, except that Ibn Numayr, said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, he said: Al-Manhal narrated to us."
"12158","(12158) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, and Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, who said: No. I tell you except what I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: O God, I seek refuge in You from inability, laziness, and cowardice. And miserliness and the torment of the grave. (Muslim 2088, Tirmidhi 3572)"
"12159","(12159) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir: On the authority of Umm Mubashir, she said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon me. May God bless him and grant him peace. I was in one of the walls of Banu al-Najjar, in which were graves of some of them who had died during the pre-Islamic era. He said: So he came out, and I heard him say: Seek refuge in God from the torment of the grave. I said, O Messenger of God, and the grave has a torment. He said: They are They will be tortured in their graves with a punishment that animals can hear. (Tabarani 25. Ahmad 6/362)"
"12160","(12160) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Awn ibn Abi Juhayf, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Bara’ ibn Azib, On the authority of Abu Ayyub: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a voice when the sun was setting, and he said: These are the voices of the Jews. She will be tortured in her graves. (Bukhari 1375. Muslim 69)"
"12161","(12161) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Anas: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge in From cowardice, miserliness, the trials of life and death, and the torment of the grave. (Nasa’i 7881. Ahmad 3/208)"
"12162","(12162) Affan narrated to us, he said: Wahib narrated to us, Musa bin Uqba narrated to us, on the authority of Umm Khalid bint Khalid, that she heard The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, seeks refuge from the torment of the grave. (Bukhari 1376. Ahmad 6/365)"
"12163","(12163) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Fatima, on the authority of Asma, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: It has been revealed to me that you will be tested in the graves, for example, or close to the trial of the Antichrist, and then one of you will come. Then it will be said to him: What did you know about this man? He said: As for the believer, he will say: He is Muhammad, he is the Messenger of God. He brought us clear evidence and guidance. We responded and followed, and it is said: Sleep righteously, for we know that you believe in God. As for the hypocrite, or the doubter, I do not know which. That is what Asma said, and he says, “I don’t know.” I heard the people say something, so I said it. (Bukhari 861, Muslim 12)"
"12164","(12164) Waki’ and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, who said: I heard Mujahid narrating on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by two graves and said: They will be punished, but they will not be punished for any great grave. One of them used to spread gossip, and as for the other, he did not cleanse himself of his urine, and Abu Muawiyah did not say, “I heard Mujahid"
"12165","(12165) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Hasan, who said: Amr and I were Ibn Al-Aas were sitting, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came out to us, carrying a piece of paper, or something similar to it, and he took cover with it. Then he urinated while sitting, so we said: You have urinated, O Messenger of God, just as a woman urinates. He said: Then we came and said: Do you not know what happened? A companion of the Children of Israel. If a man among them got on some urine, he would pinch it with a scissor, but he forbade them from doing so. So he was tortured in his grave."
"12166","(12166) Ubaidah bin Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, on the authority of Saad, that he said For his sons, that is, his sons, seek refuge in God with words that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge with. Then he mentioned the torment of the grave. (Bukhari 6374 and Tirmidhi 3567)"
"12167","(12167) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, on the authority of Saad, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the same. (Bukhari 6374)"
"12168","(12168) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, Yazid bin Kaysan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He passed The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on a grave, and he stood over it and said: Bring me two newspapers. He placed one of them by His head, and the other at his feet, and it was said to him: O Messenger of God, will that benefit him? He said: Perhaps it will lighten some of the torment of the grave for him, as long as we pray for him. (Ahmad 2/441)"
"12169","(12169) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Shayban, he said: Bahr ibn Marar told me, on the authority of his grandfather Abu Bakra, he said: I was walking with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he passed by two graves and said: They will punish whoever comes to me. With a newspaper? So I and a man stayed ahead of us, and we brought it. He said: He split it at the top, and planted one on this one, and on that one. And he said: Perhaps it will relieve them of what remains of their urine. Indeed, they will be tortured for their absence and urine."
"12170","(12170) Suleiman bin Harb narrated to us, Abu Salma Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Badali, on the authority of Habib bin Abu Jubayrah, on the authority of Ali bin Sayabah: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a grave where its companion was being tortured, and he said: The companion of this grave will be tortured in a great way. Then he called for a piece of newspaper and placed it on his grave, then said: Perhaps It relieves her of what is wet. (Musnad 595. Ahmad 4/172)"
"12171","(12171) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, greeted two graves, and he said: They will be tortured, but they will not be tortured in a grave way. As for one of them, he did not hide himself from it. urine, and as for the other one, he was walking around with gossip, then he took a damp leaf, divided it into two halves, then planted it in Each grave was one, so they said: O Messenger of God, why did you do this? He said: Perhaps He will make it easy for them as long as they do not become weary."
"12172","(12172) Waki` narrated to us, Al-Amash narrated to us, I heard Mujahid narrating on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said something like it, except for Waki’, who said: So he called for a wet Asib."
"12173","(12173) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: When a man is brought into his grave If he is one of the people of happiness, God will confirm him with a firm statement. Then he will be asked, “What are you?” and he will say, “I am the servant of God, alive and dead.” And I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. He said, and it is said, “Thus was I?” He said, and it is expanded. May his grave be upon him as long as God wills, and a door to Paradise will be opened for him, and some of its spirit and fragrance will enter upon him until he is resurrected. As for the other, he will be brought in his grave and it will be said to him, “You are not” three times, and he will say, “I do not know,” and it will be said to him, “No, I know” three times. Then his grave will be narrowed until his sides separate, or touch, and serpents will be sent upon him from the side of the grave and destroy him. And whenever he panics and shouts, he is suppressed with a muzzle made of iron, or made of fire, and a door to Hell is opened for him."
"12174","(12174) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib {May God strengthen those who Believe in the word that is firm in the life of this world. He said: Confirmation in the life of this world when the two angels come to the man in the grave. They said to him: Who is your Lord? He said: My Lord, God. They said: What is your religion? He said: My religion is Islam. They said: Who is your prophet? My Prophet Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: That is stability in the life of this world. (Bukhari 1369, Abu Dawud 4717)"
"12175","(12175) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Suddi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he raised him up, he said: To hear the beating of their sandals when they turn away, turning back. (Ibn Hibban 3118 and Bazzar 873)"
"12176","(12176) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, on the authority of Nabih, he said: I heard Abu Sa’id say There is no funeral procession that does not call upon its attendants, if she is a believer, and God is satisfied with her. She says, “Hurry with me,” even if she is an unbeliever. And God is displeased with her. She said, “Radoni.” There is nothing but the heavy ones who hear it, and if a person hears it, he will be alarmed and submissive. (Abdul Razzaq 6250)"
"12177","(12177) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Tamim, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Salamah, who said: He came A man came to Abu al-Darda’ while he was sick, and he said: O Abu al-Darda’, you have arrived on the verge of parting with this world, so give me something. God has benefited me through it, and I remind you of it. He said: You are of a healthy mother, so perform the prayer and pay the zakat of your wealth. It was for you. Fast Ramadan and avoid immoral acts, then give good tidings. He said: Then the man repeated the same to Abu al-Darda’, and he told him a parable. So, Shu`ba said: I think he repeated it three times, and Abu Darda responded to him three times, so the man shook off his robe. And he said: {Indeed, those who conceal the proofs and the guidance We have sent down, after We have made them clear to the people in the Book} until his saying {And those who curse will curse them} Then Abu al-Darda’ said: Ali the man, so he came and Abu al-Darda’ said: What did you say? He said: I was a man who taught you from Knowledge is what I do not have, so she wanted to tell me about what God has benefited me with, but she did not respond to me except one word, so he said to him: Abu Al-Darda’: Sit down, then understand what I am saying. Where have you been since the day when you had no land except the width of two cubits by the length of it? Four cubits. Your family, those who did not like to be separated from you, those who sat with you, and your brothers accepted you, and they were strong over you. lofty buildings, then they piled dust on you, then they left you to do that, then there came to you two black, blue, and curly angels. Their names are Munkar and Nakir. So he made you sit down, then he asked you: What are you or what are you doing? Or what do you say about this? If you say: By God, I don’t know. I heard the people saying something, so I said, “By God, you have been rejected and disgraced.” And you are gone, and if you say: Muhammad is the Messenger of God, God has sent down His Book to you, and I believe in it and in what He brought, then by God it is true. You were saved, you were converted, and you were not able to do that except with God’s confirmation, despite the distress and fear you see."
"12178","(12178) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn al-Asbaani, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The children of Muslims are in a mountain between Abraham and Sarah, and they are taken care of for them."
"12179","(12179) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, who said: I heard Al-Baraa’ saying: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: When Abraham died, he said: Indeed, he has a wet nurse in Paradise. (Ahmad 4/300, Ibn Saad 139)"
"12180","(12180) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He has a wet nurse. In Paradise, the rest of his breastfeeding will be completed. (Abdul Razzaq 14013. Ahmad 4/297)"
"12181","(12181) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, may God bless him and grant him peace. Sixteen months old (Abu Dawud 3180)"
"12182","(12182) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he did not see any harm in sprinkling water on the grave."
"12183","(12183) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: There is no harm in sprinkling water on the grave."
"12184","(12184) Harami bin Amara told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Bakr, who said: I was at a funeral and with us was Ziyad bin Jubayr. Ibn Hayya, when they leveled the grave, water was poured over it, and a man went to touch it and repair it, and he said: Ziyad is forced to The hands touch the grave after water has been sprinkled on it."
"12185","(12185) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Zazan: on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace at the funeral of a man from the Ansar. We went to the grave and when he was dead, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, and we sat around him as if there were birds over our heads, and in his hand was a stick to play with, so he raised his head and said: Seek refuge in God from the torment of the grave three times, or twice. Then he said: If the believing servant is in a state of This world and the arrival of the Hereafter. Angels with white faces descended to him from the sky, as if their faces were the sun. They will sit there as far as the eye can see, with them a shroud from the shrouds of Paradise and spices from the spices of Paradise, then an angel will come. Then he will sit by his head and say: O pure soul, come out to God’s forgiveness and satisfaction, and you will come out. It flows just as a drop of water flows from a watering can, and they take it, but when they take it, they do not leave it in their hand for even the blink of an eye. They took her and put her in that shroud and that spice, and from her came out as perfume smelling of musk. Found on the face of the earth,Then they go up with it, but they do not pass it past any of the angels except that they say: What is this beautiful soul? They say: This is so-and-so, son of so-and-so, with the best of the names he was called by in this world, until they end up with them. To the lowest heavens, then it will be opened and it will be opened for them, and from every heaven those closest to it will receive it, to the next heavens. Until He takes him to the seventh heaven. He said: Then God Almighty says: Write the letter of My servant in two upper heavens in the heavens. Fourth: Return him to the earth, for from it I created them, and from it I will return them, and from it I will bring them out another time. Then his soul will be returned to his body, and two angels will come to him and sit with him, and they will say to him: Who is your Lord? So he says: My Lord, God. They say to him: What is your religion? So he says, “My religion is Islam,” and they say to him: “Who is this man who was sent among you?” He says: He is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then they say: What did you do to him? So he says: I read the Book of God and believed in it and believed in it. Then a herald will call from the heavens, “My servant has spoken the truth, so give him a bed of Paradise.” And clothe him from Paradise, and open for him a door to Paradise, so some of its perfume and spirit will come to him, and it will be made spacious for him. His grave extends to one's eyes, and a man with a beautiful face, well-dressed, and a pleasant smell comes to him and says: Give good news of that. It pleases you,This is your day that you were promised. He will say: Who are you? And your face is the face that brings goodness, and he says: I am your good deed, and he says: My Lord, establish the course, my Lord, establish the course. Until I return to my family and property, and if the disbeliever servant is cut off from this world and seeking the Hereafter, he descends To Him from the heavens are angels with black faces, wearing sackcloth, until they sit beside Him as far as the eye can see. He said: Then He will come. The angel of death, until he sits at his head and says: O evil soul, come out to the wrath of God. And he became angry. He said: Then it dispersed throughout his body. He said: Then it came out, and the veins and sinews were cut with it, just as the robes of wet wool are removed. So they took it, and when they had taken it, they did not leave it in their hand for the blink of an eye until they had taken it and put it in Those sackcloths, and from them comes out as if a dead body was found on the surface of the ground, and they go up with it, but they do not pass by it. Upon one of the angels, they said: What is this evil spirit? They say: So-and-so, son of so-and-so, by the ugliest of names with which he was called in this world until he ended up with them. the lowest heavens, and they ask for it, but it will not be opened for it.Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: “The gates of heaven will not be opened for them, nor will they enter Paradise until the camel enters.” In the name of the tailor} He said: Then God Almighty will say: Write the letter of My servant in a prisoner in the lower earth, and return him to The earth, for from it I created you and to it I will return them, and from it I brought them out another time. He said: So his spirit is cast out. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: {And whoever associates partners with God, it is as if he had fallen from the sky and birds had snatched him or He was carried away by the wind in a deep place. He said: Then his soul will be returned to his body, and two angels will come to him and sit with him. Then they say to him: Who is your Lord? He says: Aha, I don’t know. And they say: What is your religion? He says: Aha, I don’t know. He said: Then a herald calls from the heavens. Spread a blanket for him from the Fire, and clothe him from the Fire, and open for him a door to the Fire. He said: So he came to him from its heat and poisons. And his grave will be constricted until his ribs are divided into one another, and there will come to him a man with an ugly face, foul-smelling clothes, stinking The wind, and He says: Rejoice in that which is bad for you. This is your day which you were promised. So He says: Who are you? Your face is the face. Who brings evil? So He says: I am your evil deed. So He says: My Lord, do not perform the Hour. O Lord, do not perform the Hour."
"12186","(12186) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, Al-Manhal narrated to us, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Al-Bara’, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said something similar to it and added to it: And the prisoner is under the lower ground."
"12187","(12187) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: And it is a sweeter smell than musk. He said: Then the angels who take her will ascend with it, and they will meet them. Your angels are below the water, and they say, “Who is this with you?” They say, “So-and-so, son of so-and-so.” And they remind him of his best deeds, so they say, May God bless you and may God bless those who are with you. He said, “And the gates of heaven will be opened for him.” He said, “And his face will shine.” He said, “And the Lord will come to him.” And on his face there is proof like the sun. He said, “As for the other, his soul emerges as it were from the carcass, and it ascends with it.” They will take her. He said, “And your angels will meet them below the heavens, and they will say, ‘Who is this with you?’ and they will say, ‘This is so-and-so’.” And they remind him of the worst of his deeds. He said, and they say, “Reject him, but God has not wronged him in the least.” Abu Musa read, “And they will not enter Jinnah, such that the camel enters the eye of the tailor.)"
"12188","(12188) Zayd bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The dead will hear the beating of their sandals when they turn away from him, and if he is a believer, the prayer will be at his head and Zakat was on his right hand, fasting was on his left hand, and doing good deeds was charity, prayer, kindness, and good deeds. The people are at his feet, and he comes from his head, and you say the prayer, “There is no entrance before me,” and he comes from his right, and you say the zakat. There is no entrance before me, and it comes from his left, so he says: Fasting is an entrance before me, and it comes from before his feet, so he says: “Fāl.” Better than honesty, prayer, kindness, and kindness to people, there is no entrance before me. He says, and it is said to him, “Sit,” and he sits. It has appeared. To him, the sun has approached the setting, so he is told, “Tell us about what we ask you about.” He says, “Leave me so that I may pray.” He is told, “You are You will do so, so tell us what we ask you. He says, And what you ask me, they say. Did you see this man who was among you? What do you say? And what do you bear witness to? He said, “Muhammad,” and it is said to him, “Yes,” and he says, “I bear witness that he is the Messenger of God and that he will come.” With clear proofs from God, so we have confirmed him, and it will be said to him: On that you lived, and on that you died, and on that you will be resurrected, God willing. Come, come,Then his grave will be widened for him by seventy cubits, and it will be illuminated for him. Then a door to Paradise will be opened for him, and it will be said to him: Look at what God has prepared for you therein, and your joy and happiness will increase. Then a door to Hell will be opened for him, and it will be said to him: That. Your seat and what God has prepared for you therein. If you disobey Him, He will increase your joy and happiness, then He will put a breath in the pleasant breeze. A green bird clings to the trees of Paradise, and the body is returned to where it started from the dust. This is the saying of God Almighty: {God establishes Those who believe in the firm saying in this life and in the hereafter} Muhammad said, Omar bin Al-Hakam bin Thawban said: Then it is said He slept and slept like a bride’s sleep. No one would wake him except the people most beloved to him, until God Almighty resurrects him. Muhammad said, Abu Salamah said, Abu Hurairah said, and if he is an unbeliever, then he should be brought by his head, and nothing will be found for him, then He comes to his right and nothing is found of him, then he comes to his left and nothing is found of him, then he comes By his feet, but nothing was found on him. So it was said to him: Sit down. He sat down, frightened and terrified. It was said to him: Tell us about what We ask you about him? He says: What are you asking me about? It will be said: Have you seen this man who was among you? What do you say about him and what do you testify against him?He said: So he says: What man? He said: It is said: He who is among you does not follow his name. It is said: Muhammad. He says: I do not know. I heard the people saying something, so I said: As they said: It will be said, “You lived for that,” “You died upon that,” and “You will be resurrected upon that,” God willing. Then a door will be opened for him. Hellfire, and it will be said to him: This is your seat and what God has prepared for you therein. Then his grief and despair will increase, then a door will be opened for him. Paradise, and it will be said to him, “This is your seat from it,” and his grief and grief will increase, then his grave will be narrowed until it becomes different. His ribs, and that is the straitened livelihood of which God Almighty said: {Indeed, he will have a straitened livelihood, and We will gather him on the Day of Resurrection. Blind}"
"12189","(12189) Waki` narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Sarraj, on the authority of Nafi`, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that He heard a man at a funeral saying: Raise up in the name of God. Ibn Umar said: Do not say, Raise up in the name of God, for God’s name is over everything. And say: Raise in the name of God."
"12190","(12190) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah al-Muzani, who said: So You carried the bed, so say: In the name of God and glorify Him."
"12191","(12191) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, who said: When he was pregnant, he said: In the name of God and glorify what He carried"
"12192","(12192) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Aisha and Ibn Abbas, that Abu Bakr kissed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, after His death (Bukhari 5711. Tirmidhi 390)"
"12193","(12193) Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: He kissed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace when he was dead, and I saw his tears streaming down his cheeks. (Tirmidhi 989. Abu Dawud 3155)"
"12194","(12194) Marhum bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Juniy, on the authority of Yazid bin Babanus, on the authority of Aisha, That Abu Bakr kissed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, after his death. (Ibn Saad 265)"
"12195","(12195) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khalid, on the authority of Abdullah al-Bayhi, the client of the family of al-Zubayr, that Abu Bakr came To the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, after he was arrested, and he uncovered his face and leaned on him and kissed him, and said: May my father be sacrificed for you. And my mother, what a good life you have and what a good death you have."
"12196","(12196) Affan narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, he said: Asim bin Bhaddalah narrated to us, he said: When Abu Wa’il died, he kissed Abu Her forehead."
"12197","(12197) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Zayd bin Nashit, on the authority of Hussein bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Abu Khalid Al-Walbiyy, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, consoled a man and said: May God have mercy on him and reward you."
"12198","(12198) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Shimr, that when he comforted an injured person, he would say: Be patient for the judgment of God. Your Lord"
"12199","(12199) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Mawdud, on the authority of Talha ibn Ubaid Allah ibn Kariz, who said: He who comforts an afflicted person. God has covered him with a robe with which he is honored, meaning he is envied."
"12200","(12200) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Nafidh, who said: I said to Ubaid Allah bin Ubad, “How were these two?” The two sheikhs, Uzzayan, meaning Ibn al-Zubayr and Ubaid bin Umair, said: They used to say: May God reward you. May God reward you with prayers. And His mercy, and He made you among those who are guided, and He followed you as His servants followed the prophets and the righteous."
"12201","(12201) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour ibn Safiyya, who said: I heard a man called Yusuf narrating My mother, he said: Whoever shrouds a dead person is like one who shrouds a young person until he is old."
"12202","(12202) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, he said: An informant informed me, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever shrouds a dead person, God will cover him with the fineness and silk of Paradise. (Hakim 354)"
"12203","(12203) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: A man came to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: My mother has lost herself, and if she spoke, she would give in charity. What reward would she have? I gave in charity on her behalf. He said: Yes. (Bukhari 2760, Muslim 51)"
"12204","(12204) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, Al-Aas ibn Wail used to order during the pre-Islamic period that his body be slaughtered. And Hisham bin Al-Aas sacrificed his share of that, fifty corpses. Did he sacrifice it for him? He said: If only your father had agreed By monotheism, then she fasted on his behalf, or gave alms on his behalf, or set her free on his behalf until he attained that. (Bayhaqi 279)"
"12205","(12205) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, who said: If he had given in charity, on behalf of the dead, the sheep would have followed him."
"12206","(12206) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Saad ibn Ubadah asked for a fatwa. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a vow to his mother. She died before she could fulfill it, so he said: Fulfill it on her behalf.

(Bukhari 6698 and Muslim 1260)"
"12207","(12207) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of my father Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: A man is ascending a flight of stairs, and he says: What is this? It is said with a request for forgiveness. Your children after you are yours. (Ahmad 2/509, Bayhaqi 79)"
"12208","(12208) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: The man will be raised By his son’s supplication for him after him."
"12209","(12209) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ata’, and on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zayd ibn He converted to Islam. They said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, should I be freed on behalf of my father since he has died? He said: Yes. (Abdul Razzaq 16340)"
"12210","(12210) Waki’ narrated to us, Ibn Rawwad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Dinar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Among the righteousness after righteousness is that you pray for them with your prayers, and to fast on their behalf with your fasting, and to give alms. About them and your charity."
"12211","(12211) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata, who said: He shall pay off, on the authority of the dead, four quarters of emancipation. And charity, Hajj and Umrah."
"12212","(12212) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata’, who said: After his death, the deceased is followed by emancipation. And Hajj and charity."
"12213","(12213) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ata, on the authority of Ibn Buraida, on the authority of his father, he said: I was He was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a woman came to him and said: My mother was required to fast for two months. Would it be sufficient for me to fast on her behalf? He said: Yes. She said: My mother had never performed Hajj. Would it be sufficient for me to fast for her? He said: Yes 

(Muslim 158. Ahmad 351)"
"12214","(12214) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ata’, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, that Al-Hasan And Al-Hussein was freed on behalf of Ali after his death."
"12215","(12215) Shababi bin Siwar narrated to us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Saad bin Sinan, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Patience in the first shock. (Tirmidhi 987. Ibn Majah 1596)"
"12216","(12216) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It was said: Patience is only at the first time of adversity."
"12217","(12217) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Uqaili, on the authority of Abu Salma Al-Homsi, who said: Patience when confronted The first"
"12218","(12218) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Thabit, who said: I heard Anas say that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Patience is in or at the first shock. (Bukhari 1252, Abu Dawud 3115)"
"12219","(12219) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Patience at the first shock."
"12220","(12220) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Habib ibn al-Shahid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that Zayd ibn Thabit asked Uthman’s permission. Concerning the exhuming of graves that were in the mosque of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he gave him permission, so he exhumed them and took them out of the mosque. He said, “It was only left in the mosque because there were few slaves among the people.”"
"12221","(12221) Zayd bin Harun told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, on the authority of Anas, that the Mosque of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. It belonged to Banu al-Najjar, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to them: “Take advantage of him.” They said: We do not seek a price for it except from God. And there were in it graves of the polytheists, and palm trees, and plowing. So he commanded plowing, so he ploughed and with palm trees. So it was cut up and the graves were dug up. (Bukhari 428. Muslim 10)"
"12222","(12222) Abu Usama told us, Ismail told us, Qays told us, he said, On the day of Marwan Talhay, he shot an arrow at the camel. I kneeled on him and he died, so we buried him on the shore of Al-Kala’, and some of his family saw him. He said, “Will you not relieve me from this water? She was drowned three times, he said, so they exhumed him and bought him a house from the family of Abu Bakr for ten thousand and buried him. There it is."
"12223","(12223) Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: The dead person is tortured in his grave for wailing. (Bukhari 1292. Muslim 639)"
"12224","(12224) Waki’ told us, Sa’id bin Ubaid and Muhammad bin Qais Al-Asadi told us, they heard it from Ali bin Rabi’ah. Al-Walbiyy, he said: The first person to wail over Kufa was Qarza bin Ka’b Al-Ansari, then Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba stood up and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever wails for him, he will be punished in his grave for what he wailed for.

(Bukhari 1291, Muslim 644)"
"12225","(12225) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ubaid, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Walid bin Ubadah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever wailed for him, he will be punished for what he wailed for on the Day of Resurrection. (Ahmed 61)"
"12226","(12226) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Umm Atiyya, who said when the verse was revealed {When the believing women come to you He pledges his allegiance to you) until his saying: {And do not disobey you in what is right} She said: It was part of him wailing, so I said: O Messenger of God, except the So-and-so, for they made me happy during the pre-Islamic era. He said: Except the family of so-and-so. (Bukhari 4892. Muslim 32)"
"12227","(12227) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Abdullah - the client of the Saba’is - on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Umm Salama, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, {And let him not disobey you in what is right.} He said: Noah. (Tirmidhi 3307, Ahmad 320)"
"12228","(12228) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: What causes disbelief in people is whining and disputing lineages. (Muslim 121, Tirmidhi 1001)"
"12229","(12229) Affan narrated to us, Aban Al-Attar narrated to us, Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd, on the authority of Abu Salam, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ash’ari, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: There are four in my nation from the pre-Islamic era who do not They will leave you with pride in accounts, and discrediting lineages, and seeking rain by the stars and lamentations, and lamenting if you do not repent of Before her death, she will be raised on the Day of Resurrection wearing a garment of tar and a shield of scabs. (Muslim 29. Ahmad 5/342)"
"12230","(12230) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: It is forbidden to wail. (Abu Dawud 2069; Abd al-Razzaq 1079)"
"12231","(12231) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Ali, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace And peace be upon him, he forbade lamentation."
"12232","(12232) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem: (And let him not disobey you in what is right) He said: Noah."
"12233","(12233) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hilal ibn Khabab, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, who said: Mourning over the dead is from The matter of the ignorant"
"12234","(12234) Waki’ narrated to us, Ishaq bin Othman Al-Kalabi narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Rahman bin Atiyya. Al-Ansari, on the authority of his mother, said: I said to her, “What is the good deed that you were forbidden from doing?” She said: “Nihahah.” (Ahmad 5/851 Abu Dawud 1132)"
"12235","(12235) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam: (And let them not disobey you in what is right) He said: They will not be divided. They will not scratch their faces, nor will they spread their hair, nor will they call upon a woe."
"12236","(12236) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Razi, on the authority of al-Rabi`, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah (And do not disobey you in what is right) He said: In every matter, he agreed to obey God, but he did not approve of his Prophet being obeyed in disobedience to God."
"12237","(12237) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qasim al-Ju’fi, who said: I heard al-Sha’bi say, “Cursed are the one who mourns and the one who is held captive.”"
"12238","(12238) Ali bin Hashim and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I have only forbidden lamentation. (Tirmidhi 1005)"
"12239","(12239) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: Abu Al-Bakhtari was a gentle man and used to listen. Lamentation"
"12240","(12240) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Salih, he said: I see it on the authority of Abu Wa’il, that he used to listen to wailing. And he makes you cry."
"12241","(12241) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of his father, he said, when Omar was injured, he made Suhaib said to him, “And his brother.” He said: Then Omar said to him, Suhaib, “Did you not know that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The dead will be tortured because of the crying of the living. (Bukhari 1290, Muslim 19)"
"12242","(12242) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Ubaid Allah bin Umar narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah, that Hafsiya wept for Omar, He said: Wait, my children. Did you not know that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The dead will be tortured because of the crying of his family? Aliyah

(Muslim 16 Ahmad 1/36)"
"12243","(12243) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Subaih, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Sirin, he said They mentioned, according to Imran bin Al-Husayn, that a dead person is tortured due to the crying of a living person. They said: How can he be tortured due to the crying of a living person? He said he had said it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Ahmad 4/437)"
"12244","(12244) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Indeed, the dead are tortured because of the crying of the living. (Bukhari 1286. Muslim 24)"
"12245","(12245) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, he said: Umm said When Abu Salama died, I said, “A stranger, and in a strange land, I would have made you cry with a cry that is spoken of.” So I was prepared. To cry when a woman came from Upper Egypt wanting to make me happy, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, met her and said: Do you want to bring Satan into a house from which God has expelled him twice? She said: So I stopped crying, so I did not cry. (Muslim 10. Ahmad 6/289)"
"12246","(12246) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha said: When she came and Ja`far died, we saw sadness on the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man entered upon him. He said: O Messenger of God, the women are crying. He said: So return to them and silence them. If they show it, then search their faces. Dust said: Aisha said: So I said to myself, By God, I will not abandon myself, nor will you be obedient to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted you. (Bukhari 1299, Muslim 644)"
"12247","(12247) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that it was said to her that Ibn Omar was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: The dead are tortured by the crying of the living, so she said, “Woe to Abu Abd al-Rahman. He only said: The family of the dead will weep over him, and he will be punished for his crime. (Bukhari 3978, Muslim 25)"
"12248","(12248) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hijri, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, he said: He saw the women He said: Do not be hesitant, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from inheriting. (Ibn Majah 1592. Tayalisi 825)"
"12249","(12249) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Isa, on the authority of Jabr bin Atik, on the authority of His uncle, he said, I entered with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, over a man from the Ansar and his family who were crying, so I said, “Are you crying over him?” And this is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Let them cry as long as With them, when necessary, they do not cry. (Abu Dawud 3102. Ahmad 5/446)"
"12250","(12250) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Asama bin Zaid, who said, “The eyes of the Messenger of God brought tears to God.” May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when he brought his daughter Zainab while her soul was rattling as if she was in a state of pain. He said, so he cried. He said: so he said His: A man who made you cry, even though you were forbidden from crying, and he said: This is only a mercy that God placed in the hearts of His servants. May God have mercy on His merciful servants. (Muslim 636. Ahmad 5/204)"
"12251","(12251) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took Peace be upon him, and he greeted Abdul Rahman bin Awf, so he went out to the palm trees and brought Abraham, and he was generous with himself. So he was placed in his lap, and he said: O my son, I do not give you anything from God, and his eyes shed tears, so Abd al-Rahman said to him Are you weeping, O Messenger of God, or have you not forbidden you from crying? He said: I have only forbidden lamentation, two foolish, immoral voices. A voice with its melody of amusement and play, and the psalms of the devil, and a voice at a calamity, one that scratches faces and rips open pockets, And a devil appeared to me. This is only mercy, and he who does not have mercy will not have mercy. O Abraham, had it not been a matter of truth and a promise. It is the truth, and the path is coming, and the last of us will join the first of us to grieve for you more severely than this, and we are truly saddened by you. The eye weeps and the heart grieves, but we do not say anything that displeases the Lord."
"12252","(12252) Waki’ narrated to us, Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, he said: The hadith of Ibn Omar, the dead are tormented by the crying of the living, so she said: Abu Abd al-Rahman wailed just as he did on the day of the heart of Badr. The Messenger only said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: He will be punished and his family will weep for him. (Ahmed 6/209)"
"12253","(12253) Shababah bin Siwar narrated to us, Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. A boy was born to me that night, and I named him after Abraham’s father. He said: Then he gave him to Umm Saif. A strong woman in Medina called Abu Saif. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, set off and I went with him. So we came across Abu Saif blowing on a pipe, and the house was filled with smoke, so I hastened to walk in front of the Prophet. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, until he came to Abu Saif, and I said: O Abu Saif, hold you back, hold you back. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has come. May God bless him and grant him peace. He held him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called the boy and held him to him, and said, “Whatever God wills.” He says, Anas said: I saw him distressed by himself, he said: Then tears came to the eyes of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The eyes bring tears and the heart is sad, and we only say what pleases our Lord, and we are in you. Abraham is sad. (Muslim 62. Abu Dawud 3118)"
"12254","(12254) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Usama ibn Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God returned On the day of Uhud, he heard the wives of Banu Abd al-Ashhal crying over their loss, and he said: But Hamza has no weeping. Then the women of the Ansar came and wept over Hamza, so he fell asleep and woke up and said: Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh! So let them return, and do not weep for anyone who perishes after today. (Ahmad 2/40 Hakim 194)"
"12255","(12255) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Zaid, he said: Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib narrated to me, Ikrimah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abbas used to say, “Memorize this hadith. One of the daughters of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was dying.” He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed her on his hand and placed her head on his breast, and she drove until she finished. So he put her down while he was crying. He said: Then Umm Ayman cried out, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I do not see you crying when... The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: First, I see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, crying. He said: I did not I cry, but we have mercy on you. (Ahmad 1/273)"
"12256","(12256) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, my father narrated to me, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Waqqas, on the authority of Aisha Umm The believers said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr and Omar attended the funeral of Saad bin Muadh. The soul of Muhammad is in his hand. I know that Omar’s crying is better than Abu Bakr’s crying while I am in my room. She said: So they were as God said. {Merciful among them}, Alqamah said: How did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do what he did? He said: She was His eyes do not shed a tear for anyone, but when he was there, he was only holding his beard. (Ahmad 6/141; Ibn Hibban 6439)"
"12257","(12257) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: I brought Omar with the obituary of Nu’man. Ibn Muqrin put his hand on his head and started crying."
"12258","(12258) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hajri, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: If a woman cries, or an eye sheds tears There is no problem, but we have been forbidden from inheriting."
"12259","(12259) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar was in the market and a stone was called to him. Then he let go of his beast and got up, overcome by wailing."
"12260","(12260) Waki’ narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amir bin Saad Al-Bajli, on the authority of Abu Masoud and Thabit Ibn Yazid and Qarza Ibn Ka'b said: We have been granted permission to cry over the dead in a manner other than mourning."
"12261","(12261) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad, who said: I entered upon Abu Masoud and Qarza bin Ka’b. They said: We have been given permission to cry in times of calamity. (Hakim 184. Tabarani 82)"
"12262","(12262) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amir bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Masoud and Thabit bin Zaid. Like it (Hakim 184)"
"12263","(12263) Affan told us, Wahhab told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of Wahhab bin Kaysan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr Ibn Ata’, on the authority of Salama Ibn Al-Azraq, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by at a funeral. He cried over her, and I was with him, and Omar bin Al-Khattab, and Omar stopped those who were crying at the funeral, and the Messenger of God said, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace: Leave them, O Ibn Al-Khattab, for the soul is afflicted, the eye is weeping, and the covenant is near. (Ahmad 2/408 and Abd al-Razzaq 6674)"
"12264","(12264) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Wahhab ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similarly."
"12265","(12265) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, on the authority of Nabih, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, commanded that they return the slain to their battlefields. (Abu Dawud 3157, Tirmidhi 1717)"
"12266","(12266) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: I heard a sheikh in Banu Amir, one of Banu Sawa, being called Abdullah bin Mu'iyah said: Two Muslim men were injured on the day of Ta'if. He said: So they were carried to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. When he heard that, he was sent to bury us wherever they were injured or met."
"12267","(12267) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour ibn Safiyya, on the authority of his mother, who said: I came to Aisha to console her. About a brother of hers who died in one place and was carried while he was dead and was buried in another place, so she said to myself: “Nothing about him except that I wished.” He was buried where he died."
"12268","(12268) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Buhman, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Bodies are buried where souls are taken. (Ibn Saad 293)"
"12269","(12269) Waki’ narrated to us, Al-Aswad bin Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Samir, on the authority of Bashir bin Nayk, on the authority of Bashir bin Al-Khasasiyya said that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man walking between the graves in his sandals, and he said: O companion of the two Saturdays, throw them away. (Nasa’i 2175. Abu Dawud 3222)"
"12270","(12270) Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, who said: I saw Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin walking together. Between the graves in their sandals."
"12271","(12271) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of a man called Al-Nu’man Al-Jundi, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, He disliked being drawn from the wells that were between the sides of the graves."
"12272","Abu Abdul Rahman Buqiy bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shayba told us, he said:

(12272) Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Al-Hussein said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no vow in disobedience to God, nor in what is not over Him.” The slave

(Abu Dawud 3000, Ahmad 4/433)"
"12273","(12273) Abdullah bin Numayr, and Abu Asama, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Talha bin Abdul Malik, on the authority of Al-Qasim Bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: Whoever vows to obey God, let him obey Him, and whoever vows If he disobeys God, he will not disobey you. (Bukhari 6696 and Abu Dawud 3282)"
"12274","(12274) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Zayd bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: Abdul said: God: A vow does not advance anything, nor does it delay it, but God extracts it from the miserly person, so there is no fulfillment of the vow in it. Disobedience"
"12275","(12275) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of al-Dalani, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: There is no fulfillment of a vow in Disobedience (Abdul Razzaq 15823. Ahmed 297)"
"12276","(12276) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Qays, on the authority of his maternal aunt Malaki, on the authority of Ubaidah, she said: I asked him about vows, and he said: Whatever vow was made was in obedience to God, so they fulfilled it, and whatever vow was in obedience to God, they fulfilled it. Anything of obedience to Satan, do not allow it."
"12277","(12277) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: A vow is two vows, so a vow is made to God. And Satan made a vow, so whatever it is for God is fulfillment and expiation, and whatever Satan is for there is no fulfillment or expiation."
"12278","(12278) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: The vow Two vows: whatever is for God, fulfill it, and whatever is due to disobedience, do not fulfill it, and you must make expiation."
"12279","(12279) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Amara bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: No vow of disobedience, blasphemy. Yemen"
"12280","(12280) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: A man came to Ibn Abbas, and he said: I have vowed to lie naked until the night, and he said: Satan wanted to expose your private parts. And for people to laugh at you, wear your clothes and pray two rak’ahs at the Hijr."
"12281","(12281) Affan narrated to us, he said: Aban Al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, On the authority of Thabit bin Al-Dahhak Al-Ansari, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: No man is obligated to vow anything concerning He owns it.

(Bukhari 6047, Muslim 174)"
"12282","(12282) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Thabit, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about the vow of disobedience. Is there any loyalty in it? He said: No."
"12283","(12283) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Qays, who said: Abu Bakr entered upon a woman of Ahmose’s family. In her hiding place, she started pointing at him, but did not speak to him. He said: Why does she not speak? They said: She has vowed to perform Hajj silently, so he said: Speak to me, for this is not permissible for you. This is merely an action. The pre-Islamic one"
"12284","(12284) Shababah ibn Sawwar, on the authority of Shu’bai, on the authority of Abu al-Huwarithah, or on the authority of Abu al-Juwayriyah, there is no doubt about my father’s Bakr, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Badr mentioned on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: No vow of disobedience."
"12285","(12285) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Farwa, Yazid bin Sinan, on the authority of Urwah bin Ruwaym, on the authority of Abu Tha’labiyah Al-Khushani, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: There is no fulfillment of a vow in the case of disobedience."
"12286","(12286) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both; Concerning a man who swears a vow or something forbidden, he said: He did not intend to be harsh on himself, free a slave, or fast. Two shares, or to feed sixty poor people. He said: So I asked Abraham and Mujahid, and they said: If he does not have the means, then feed ten. Poor people"
"12287","(12287) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, who said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr saying: Fulfill your vows."
"12288","(12288) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Zayd ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: No. A fulfillment of a vow to disobey God, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"12289","(12289) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd al-Dalani, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Infidelity is infidelity. Right"
"12290","(12290) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’. He said: He was asked about a man who vowed not to enter On his sister or brother, and he said: He goes in and gives alms to ten poor people."
"12291","(12291) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa Al-Muallem, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: The vow is an oath."
"12292","(12292) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The vow is an oath."
"12293","(12293) Ibn Uyaynah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Some people say: The vow is a severe oath, but it is an oath that expiates it."
"12294","(12294) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The vow is oath."
"12295","(12295) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Muhammad Al-Hanzali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Imran bin Al-Husayn, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: There is no fulfillment of a vow in anger, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath. (Taalisi 839)"
"12296","(12296) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Zubayr Al-Hanzali, on the authority of Imran bin Al-Husayn, similarly."
"12297","(12297) Mu`tamar narrated to us: I said to Ibn al-Zubair: It was narrated to you by someone who heard it from Imran. He said: No, but a man narrated to me, on the authority of Imran"
"12298","(12298) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abdullah bin Maqil, who said: The right vow is the strong one."
"12299","(12299) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Siwar, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: The expiation for a vow if it is in Disobedience, feeding ten poor people."
"12300","(12300) Abdul Rahim, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Siwar, on the authority of Talha al-Yami, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: Whoever swears an oath by a vow and breaks it, then he must atone for a heavy oath."
"12301","(12301) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: If a man says: I have to make a vow, then he does not proceed. He swore an oath and remained silent, so he made a vow."
"12302","(12302) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: A vow is something that is extracted from a miser."
"12303","(12303) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Ibn Abbas said: A vow is a strong oath."
"12304","(12304) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The vow if it is not It is called the harshest oath, and it is the harshest of expiations."
"12305","(12305) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, who said: Whoever is appointed for the sake of Allah He made a vow and he did not pronounce the name, so we vowed it."
"12306","(12306) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: If he said: He had made a vow, but he did not name it, so he had to make expiation for the woman who followed it, then the woman who followed him, then the woman who followed him."
"12307","(12307) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: It is expiation for an indefinite vow. Atonement for swearing an oath."
"12308","(12308) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Ibn Al-Musayyab, he said: If he says: I have a vow He has a vow"
"12309","(12309) Jabir bin Zayd said: If he says: I have a vow, then if he pronounces it, then that is what he said, and if he intends it, then it is what he intended, and if not It can be called something that he fasted one day, or prayed two rak'ahs."
"12310","(12310) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If he made a vow upon me, and did not pronounce a blessing, So there is a severe oath, to free a slave, or to fast for two months, or to feed sixty poor people. He said: And he said Al-Hassan: This is an oath that expiates it."
"12311","(12311) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Rafi’, on the authority of Khalid bin Zaid, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, may God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever makes a vow and does not keep it, then he must make expiation on his oath.

(Muslim 13 Abu Dawud 3316)"
"12312","(12312) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, who said: I asked them about a man who made a vow that he did not He names him, they said: He is required to make expiation."
"12313","(12313) Waki’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The vows are four: Whoever vows a vow and does not name it, then his atonement will be expiation. An oath, and whoever vows a vow of disobedience, then its expiation is an expiation for an oath. And whoever makes a vow to commit a sin that he cannot bear, its expiation will be expiated. It is expiation for an oath, and whoever makes a vow within his capacity, let him fulfill his vow. (Abu Dawud 3315. Daraqutni 2)"
"12314","(12314) Abd al-Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Ikrimah, regarding a vow that is not called an infidel, he said: Right. Thickened"
"12315","(12315) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Awn, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Jubayr, who said: A man came to Ibn Umar. So he asked him about a man who vowed to fast one day and then he agreed to break the fast, or sacrifice, and Ibn Umar said: God has commanded the fulfillment of the vow. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade fasting on this day."
"12316","(12316) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who vowed to fast on Monday and Thursday, and on that day came the day of breaking the fast, or of the sacrifice. He said: He breaks the fast. And he fasts another day in his place."
"12317","(12317) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: He fasts a day in its place, and makes expiation. Right hand"
"12318","(12318) Uqba bin Khalid Al-Sakouni told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his maternal aunt, that she was required to fast every day. All together, that day fell on the day of breaking the fast, or the sacrifice, so she asked Jabir bin Zaid, and he said: Feed a poor person."
"12319","(12319) Shabab bin Siwar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a woman who vowed to fast every day. They gathered that day to be the day of breaking the fast, or the day of sacrifice, and they said: You make up a day in its place and make expiation for it."
"12320","(12320) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman ibn Abi Dawud, who said: Ata’ ibn Abi Rabah was asked about a man who made He must fast for two consecutive months, and he will overtake him if he sacrifices the sacrifice, or if he breaks the fast, he said: He breaks the fast, then he builds on it. Fasting"
"12321","(12321) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ali, He said: The expiation for an oath is feeding ten poor people, each poor person being given half a saa’."
"12322","(12322) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman and Abu Khaled al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hout, on the authority of those who told him, on the authority of Aisha. She said: We give half a saa’ of wheat, or a saa’ of dates, as expiation for swearing an oath."
"12323","(12323) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Yasar bin Numayr, he said: Omar said to me: I swear Shall I not give people something, then it will appear to me and I will give it to them? If I do that, I will feed ten poor people on my behalf. Between every poor person is a saa of wheat, or a saa of dates for each poor person."
"12324","(12324) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab regarding the expiation of oaths, he said: He is condemned for every Poor person."
"12325","(12325) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The expiation for an oath and an oath is half. A saa' for every poor person."
"12326","(12326) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Every expiation performed by a zihar, or someone else, must be paid. Half a saa' of righteousness as expiation."
"12327","(12327) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The expiation of an oath is one who is condemned, or one who eats it. Madaum"
"12328","(12328) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: I said: All of them? He said: No, give them two mudds, a mudd for their food and a mudd for their sustenance."
"12329","(12329) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, that he said about feeding the poor as expiation. Al-Dhahar said: For every poor person there is a mudd of wheat and a mudd of dates."
"12330","(12330) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: For every poor person there is a mudd of Wheat"
"12331","(12331) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, who said: I asked Jabir bin Zayd about expiation for swearing an oath, and he said: Feeding ten poor people, a single shuttle for every person."
"12332","(12332) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, regarding the expiation of an oath: a shuttle of his food and a shuttle. Edamah"
"12333","(12333) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Yasar bin Numayr, he said: He said: I am in charge of a matter. Muslims, if you see that I have sworn an oath that I have not fulfilled, then feed ten poor people on my behalf, for every poor person. Half a saa' of wheat, or a saa' of barley, or a saa' of dates."
"12334","(12334) Ibn Fudayl and Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, regarding the expiation of an oath: A wonderful tide is eternal."
"12335","(12335) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, he said: A mudd of wheat for every poor person."
"12336","(12336) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that if he broke his oath, he would feed Ten poor people, for each poor person a mudd of wheat in the first mudd."
"12337","(12337) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Mudd."
"12338","(12338) Sufyan bin Uyaynah and Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar. He said about the expiation of an oath, a mud of land."
"12339","(12339) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Al-Qasim and Salem regarding the expiation of oaths, They said: A mudd for every poor person."
"12340","(12340) Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, regarding feeding the poor: a handful of wheat."
"12341","(12341) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughul, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Mudd."
"12342","(12342) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: One is obligatory."
"12343","(12343) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he said regarding expiation of the poor: He pluralized them once. So He satisfies them."
"12344","(12344) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Zaid Abi Muslimama, who said: I asked Jabir bin Zaid about feeding The poor in the expiation of an oath. He said: Eat it. I said: Al-Hassan says: A shuttle. So I said: What do you see in a shuttle? Righteousness? He said: A land transport is not sufficient."
"12345","(12345) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of an alcoholic person, who said regarding the expiation of an oath: He feeds ten poor people as God Almighty said, “Until He satisfies them.”"
"12346","(12346) Yahya bin Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Ayyub narrated to me, on the authority of Humaid; Anas fell ill before he died and was unable to fast, so he was gathering thirty poor people and feeding them. Bread and meat he ate at once."
"12347","(12347) Mu`tamar narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the expiation of an oath, he said: He feeds one bitter person with bread and meat once until he is satisfied."
"12348","(12348) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, who said: He eats them in the morning and in the evening."
"12349","(12349) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Lunch and dinner."
"12350","(12350) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: To a woman, you are responsible for the adornment of so-and-so’s wife, so it is not With something"
"12351","(12351) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr ibn Haram, who said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked about a man, and he said: To his wife: You are to me like my mother’s womb. He said: The belly and the back are in the same position as the back."
"12352","(12352) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about a woman with a heavy head who slept with her. Then he died. He said: Would it be better for her soul to make expiation by freeing a slave, or to fast for two consecutive months? I said: If she menstruates, he says: This is what is necessary for women to make up the days of their menstruation when they have finished."
"12353","(12353) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a woman kills a person by mistake and fasts, then she menstruates. She spent a day in her place."
"12354","(12354) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Abi Ayyub narrated to us, saying: Yazid bin Abi narrated to us. Habib, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: As for the woman, she fasts, and when she menstruates, she completes what remains."
"12355","(12355) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a woman who was obligated to seclude herself and her menstruation overtook her. He said: She must make up the number of days during which she menstruated."
"12356","(12356) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a woman fasts in expiation for swearing three oaths, days, so she menstruated before completing her fast, so she should fast for three days."
"12357","(12357) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever swears an oath by a surah of the Qur’an, then he swears an oath of patience with every verse of it. Whoever wishes will be righteous, and whoever wills will be disobedient."
"12358","(12358) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Kanaf, who said: I was walking with Abdullah In the slave market, he heard a man swearing: No, by Surah Al-Baqarah, so Abdullah said: As for every verse of it, there is an oath upon him."
"12359","(123598) Ibn Fudayl and Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi al-Dhudhayl. On the authority of Abdullah bin Hanzala, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Whoever swears an oath by a surah of the Qur’an, he must swear it with every verse of it."
"12360","(12360) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Sahl ibn Munjab, who said: Whoever swears by a surah of the Qur’an will meet God. As many as her sins."
"12361","(12361) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Whoever swears by a surah of the Qur’an, he must swear by every verse of it. Right, and whoever disbelieves in any of its verses disbelieves in all of it."
"12362","(12362) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah said: Whoever swears by the Qur’an, he must do it in full. Right Verse"
"12363","(12363) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he used to say: He who has slaves upon him, So he bought Nasma and said: If he carries it out from one job to another, that will suffice for him, and he who does not work will not suffice for him. As for the one who does So the one-eyed and the like, and as for the one who does not work, then the blind and the paralyzed."
"12364","(12364) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He used to hate the lame and the crippled in the neck. The obligatory"
"12365","(12365) Muhammad bin Marwan narrated to us, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: A man asked him, “Will it be sufficient for freeing a slave?” The one-eyed obligatory person? He said: My Lord, one-eyed. Then he turned around and said: The lame man is sufficient. He said: Then he said: The female companion brings the crippled person."
"12366","(12366) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He cuts the one-eyed eye."
"12367","(12367) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: The insane person does not suffice for the one on his neck."
"12368","(12368) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: Is it permissible to kill a believing slave? He is not normal, and is he lame or paralyzed to benefit from it? He refused and preferred the straight one."
"12369","(12369) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: A blind person is sufficient for expiation."
"12370","(12370) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: I asked him about the blind and the paralyzed, and he said: It is not sufficient."
"12371","(12371) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim and Ash-Shu’bi that they said: It is not sufficient in any of Obligatory child of fornication."
"12372","(12372) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, who said: A man from my family died, so he bequeathed his name. Then Nasmah found a man whose father had married his mother without his master’s permission, so she asked Ata’, and he said: He hated that."
"12373","(12373) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of So-and-so bin Amr, who said: I asked Abu Ja`far about freeing a child of adultery as an expiation for swearing an oath. He said: It is sufficient."
"12374","(12374) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, that he used to say: It suffices for what is obligatory, but the one who is not superfluous There is no guidance except through piety."
"12375","(12375) Waki’ and Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Tawus, who said: A child is sufficient Adultery with a slave"
"12376","(12376) Abu Bakr ibn Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is not sufficient for obligatory slavery."
"12377","(12377) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, and Abdullah bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed: A woman came Abu Hurairah, so I asked him about the son of a maid of hers who is not of sound mind and who has slaves over her. Would that be sufficient? He said: Yes."
"12378","(12378) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he did not consider emancipating an infidel in any way. Atonements"
"12379","(12379) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The Jew is sufficient And the Christian in the expiation of swearing an oath."
"12380","(12380) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is not sufficient to free the people of disbelief."
"12381","(12381) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A Jew and a Christian are not sufficient for freeing a slave. The obligatory"
"12382","(12382) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he was of the view that the one who manages to do so is freed in all expiations."
"12383","(12383) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus: He said: The emancipation of the one who manages it is sufficient for expiation."
"12384","(12384) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A moving one is sufficient."
"12385","(12385) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: It is not sufficient for a man freed from his back to perform expiation."
"12386","(12386) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Muhajir ibn Shammas, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: As for the one that is returned, it is not sufficient."
"12387","(12387) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Bashir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The one who manages is not sufficient."
"12388","(12388) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: As for the one who manages, it is not sufficient."
"12389","(12389) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: The mother of the child should be separated from the outside."
"12390","(12390) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Muhajir ibn Shamas, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The mother of the child should be separated from her husband."
"12391","(12391) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is sufficient for the zahar."
"12392","(12392) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Hisham."
"12393","(12393) And Ibn Idris, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Tawoos, said: The mother of the child is not sufficient in public appearance."
"12394","(12394) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The mother of the child is not sufficient in expiation."
"12395","(12395) Abd al-Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: The mother of the child is not sufficient for a zihaar."
"12396","(12396) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He did not consider freeing the child’s mother in any way. Atonements"
"12397","(12397) Abu Qattan told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad regarding the mother of the child in the expiation of zihar, he said: It is not sufficient, and he said: Ruling: Other things are more beloved to me than her, and I hope for them."
"12398","(12398) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim and Al-Shu’bi, who said: The mother of the child should not part with the slaves."
"12399","(12399) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ali, who said: The mother of the child should part from the neck."
"12400","(12400) Umar ibn Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Maimun, that a man had a bad name on him and he wanted to He emancipated a son who wrote to them, and he said: I will not emancipate anyone else."
"12401","(12401) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is not sufficient for zihar, nor is Liberation, nor killing, is the result of being written to."
"12402","(12402) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, They said: As for whoever afflicts a fetus, he must free his slaves along with the slaves."
"12403","(12403) Ghandar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: I heard him say: If a woman is struck and she miscarries a fetus, he said: His companion will be freed."
"12404","(12404) Ibn Uyaynah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar ibn Dhar, on the authority of Mujahid: A man wiped a woman’s stomach, and she had a vaginal discharge. A fetus, so Omar bin Al-Khattab ordered him to be emancipated."
"12405","(12405) Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who was obligated to feed the poor as an expiation for the tyrants, and he fed ten people, then he wanted to make a feast for them until Continuing, he said: No, until he feeds sixty poor people."
"12406","(12406) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Yaqoub, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, similarly to it."
"12407","(12407) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard Omar greeted him and said: My father and my father. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God forbids you to swear. By your fathers, and Omar said: By God, I did not swear by it, neither in memory nor in favor of it. (Bukhari 6447, Muslim 2)"
"12408","(12408) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, overtook you. Omar, peace and blessings be upon him, greeted Omar in some of his travels, and he said: And my father, and my father, and he said: God forbids you to swear By your fathers, whoever swears an oath, let him swear by God, or remain silent. (Abu Dawud 3244. Tirmidhi 1534)"
"12409","(12409) Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Samarra, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Do not swear by your fathers, nor by the tyrants. (Muslim 6. Ahmad 5/62)"
"12410","(12410) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Omar said: I narrated a hadith to a people, so I said: No, by my father. Then a man behind me said: Do not swear by your fathers. He said: Then I turned around and saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: If only One of you swore by Christ to his death, and Christ is better than your fathers. (Abdul Razzaq 15925)"
"12411","(12411) Amr bin Talha narrated to us, on the authority of Asbat bin Nasr, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Omar, He said: I swore by my father, and then there was a man behind me saying: Do not swear by your fathers. I turned around and saw that he was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Ahmed 19)"
"12412","(12412) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, who said: We were with Ibn Umar in a meeting, and he heard a man say: No, but he refused, so he threw pebbles at him and said: It was the right hand of Omar, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade it, and said: : It is polytheism. (Ahmad 2/58, Tahawi 825)"
"12413","(12413) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of al-Hasan ibn Muhammad, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: He who swears by anything other than God, or says anything other than Islam, is not one of us."
"12414","(12414) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Wabarra, who said: Abdullah said: For me to swear by God falsely is more beloved to me than If I swear by something else and I am telling the truth."
"12415","(12415) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Omar passed by Al-Zubair and he said: No. And the Ka’bah, so he raised the cloak over him and said: The Ka’bah, do you not have a mother who will feed you and give you drink?"
"12416","(12416) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father, he said: Ka’b said: You are associating others. They said: How, Abu Ishaq? He said: The man swears: No, by my father, No, by your father, No, by my life, No, by your life, No, by the sanctity of the mosque, No, by Islam. And similar words."
"12417","(12417) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: You have overtaken the people, even if a man rode his camel. Because he waited before he heard a man swear by anything other than God."
"12418","(12418) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Do not swear by your fathers, nor by the tyrants."
"12419","(12419) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awany, on the authority of Ismail bin Hisham, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mukhamirrah, he said: I don't care if you swear on a man's life, or by the cross."
"12420","(12420) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated to say: No, by your life."
"12421","(12421) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Maimun, who said: I heard him say: Indeed, God Almighty He swears by whatever He wishes of His creation, and no one has the right to swear except by God, and whoever swears by God does not lie."
"12422","(12422) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Ja’far narrated to us, on the authority of Umm Bakr bint Al-Miswar, that Al-Miswar heard His son, and he said: I have associated anything with God, or I have disbelieved in God. So he struck him, then said: Say: I ask forgiveness from God. I believe in God. , three"
"12423","(12423) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Sa’d, on the authority of his father, that He said: I swore by Al-Lat and Al-Uzza, so I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I swore by Al-Lat and Al-Uzza. He said: Say: There is no god. Except Allah, three times, and spit out from your left hand three times, and seek refuge in Allah from Satan, then do not repeat it.

(Ibn Majah 2097 and Ahmed 186)"
"12424","(12424) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, he said: It was the right hand of Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas: For my life."
"12425","(12425) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I was informed that Abu Al-Sawwar Al-Adawi said: If you hear me say: No, by God, then Or, by my life, remind me."
"12426","(12426) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If a man says: By my life, I will not do such-and-such, if He broke his oath and did the expiation."
"12427","(12427) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: My life has had a lot of idle talk."
"12428","(12428) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he disliked saying: By my life."
"12429","(12429) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala, on the authority of his father, he said: Ka’b said: You are associating others. They said: How is it? O Abu Ishaq? He said: One of you says: No by my life, no by your life."
"12430","(12430) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When a man is told, “Do you swear that you will not do such-and-such?” So he says: Yes, but he did not swear. He said: He must make expiation for an oath."
"12431","(12431) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If he says: Ali is right, then he breaks the oath, then expiation is upon him."
"12432","(12432) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If he says: I swore, and he did not swear, then he is not obligated to offer expiation."
"12433","(12433) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If he says: The man I swore, and he does not swear, then he has lied. And he swore, and if he said: I swore and lied, then he lied."
"12434","(12434) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Tamim bin Tarfi, on the authority of Adiy bin Hatim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever takes an oath and sees something better than it, let him leave his oath. And let that which is best come, and let his oath be an atonement. (Muslim 1272. Ahmad 4/256)"
"12435","(12435) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, he said: Ali bin Zayd bin Jud’an narrated to us, he said: Al-Hasan narrated to us, He said: Abdul Rahman bin Samurah told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When you took an oath, you saw what And it is better than it. So the one who is better has passed away and made amends for your right hand. (Bukhari 6422 and Abu Dawud 3271)"
"12436","(12436) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Adhinna, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever swears an oath and sees something better than it, let him take one that is better and disbelieve. On his right hand (Tabarani 873. Tayalisi 1370)"
"12437","(12437) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: Abu Bakr had not taken an oath, so he broke it, until the expiation for swearing an oath came down. He said: I do not take an oath. So I see other things better than her, unless I come to the one that is better, and my oath is atoned for."
"12438","(12438) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa`id, on the authority of al-Qasim, who said: Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, used to He swore and did not break it until this verse was revealed: {Allah will not call you to account for vain talk in your oaths}, so whenever he swore He took an oath, and he saw something else better than her. He came to the one who was better and made amends for his oath."
"12439","(12439) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: They used to say: Whoever swears an oath and sees what He is better than her, so let him give up his oath, and let him who is better come, and let him make atonement for his oath."
"12440","(12440) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I said: I swore on something else that is better than I pray. Should I make amends for my oath? He said: Yes."
"12441","(12441) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Qubaysa bin Jabir, who said: I heard Umar He says: Whoever takes an oath and sees something better than it, let him do what is better and make atonement for his oath."
"12442","(12442) Abu Dawud Al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Asim bin Al-Mundhir, he said: I asked Ubaid bin Umair, On the authority of a man who vowed not to go in on his maternal aunt, he said: He should go in on her and make amends for his oath."
"12443","(12443) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said, “Abdullah was brought with an udder and we are with him.” Then a man from among the people withdrew, and Abdullah said: Come closer. Then the man said to him: I swore that I would not eat the udder of a camel. So he said: Come closer and eat."
"12444","(12444) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubaidullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with him, that he used to disbelieve before To break his oath"
"12445","(12445) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, that Muslim bin Mukhlid and Salman were of the opinion that he would make an atonement before he To break his oath"
"12446","(12446) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, called a boy of his. So he freed him, then he broke his oath and did what he swore to him."
"12447","(12447) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to make expiation before he broke his oath."
"12448","(12448) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he used to make expiation before he broke his oath."
"12449","(12449) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad used to declare blasphemy before he broke his oath, and Al-Hasan used to say: He breaks his oath, then disbelieves."
"12450","(12450) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Kathir, that he heard a man ask Jabir bin Zaid, he said: I swore an oath other than that which was better than her. He said: Disbelieve your oath and go for the one that is better."
"12451","(12451) Abdullah bin Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Malik, who said: An oath that does not expiate, a man swears on Whoever lies intentionally, that is up to God. If He wills, He will punish him, and if He wills, He will forgive him."
"12452","(12452) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad; Regarding a man who swears on something intentionally, Hammad said: This is not expiation, and he said: The ruling: Expiation is better."
"12453","(12453) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who swears on something that he has, and does not know, then he realizes that he has it. He said: He expiates his oath. He said: And he said Giving and the ruling on that which does not constitute blasphemy: blaspheme."
"12454","(12454) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There are four oaths, so two oaths make atonement. And two right sides that will not be blasphemed: By God I will not do it, and by God I will do it. He said: So as for them you will not be blasphemed. By God I have not done it, and by God I have done it. Do not be declared a disbeliever."
"12455","(12455) Sufyan bin Uyaynah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The oath Right"
"12456","(12456) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The oath is oath, then he recited: {And they swore In God, he strived for their faith."
"12457","(12457) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I swore an oath."
"12458","(12458) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, who said: A man swore not to drink milk. His wife said, Abdullah said: It would be better for himself to make expiation for his oath."
"12459","(12459) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, regarding a man who swore an oath against another man and he swore by him. He said: I would love to He expiates his oath."
"12460","(12460) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal, that a man swore an oath against another man, but he broke his oath. Abu Al-Manhal said: Aliya: Kafr Yamanik."
"12461","(12461) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He was not seen as an infidel if he swore an oath on someone else. So he swore, saying: Unless he swears an oath. If he swears an oath and breaks his oath, then the expiation is due on him."
"12462","(12462) Yahya told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniy, on the authority of the ruling, he said: The oath is right."
"12463","(12463) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The oath Right"
"12464","(12464) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Bakr, who said: If a man swears an oath to another man and he breaks it, then the sin is upon him. The one who swore on his oath, because he only swore an oath on him out of trust in him."
"12465","(12465) Ibn Mahdi and Ubaid Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, He said: The oath is oath."
"12466","(12466) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man says: I swore against you, then it is not With something, then if he says: I swear to you by God, then it is an expiation for an oath."
"12467","(12467) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I heard him say: The oath should not be Oath until he says: I swear to God."
"12468","(12468) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man says: I swear, or I bear witness, and he does not He says: By God, it is not anything."
"12469","(12469) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If a man says: I swear, or I testify, or I swear, then it is not With an oath until he says: By God."
"12470","(12470) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, they said: If a man says: I swore, but it is not an oath until he says: By God."
"12471","(12471) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim al-Taymi, who said: If a man says: To God, or to him, a Hajj is equal, and if he says: I swear to God, or to him is a vow, it is equal, and if he says: I swear By God, or I swear by the same thing."
"12472","(12472) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Talha, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is equal for a man to He says: I swear, or I swear by God that I will perform Hajj, or I will perform Hajj for God, or I will make a vow, or I will make a vow to God."
"12473","(12473) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Concerning a man who says: I must walk to the Kaaba. He said: This is a vow, so let him walk."
"12474","(12474) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hilal, he heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab say: Whoever said, “I must walk to the Kaaba.” There is nothing to do except to say: I have a vow of walking."
"12475","(12475) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: A man from among us was made obligated to walk to the House of God regarding something. So Al-Qasim came and asked him about that, and he said: He will walk to the House."
"12476","(12476) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, who said: I asked Ata’ about a man who said: May God bless me. Right, he said: It expiates her."
"12477","(12477) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: If Ibn Umar swore, he would feed a mudd, and if he vowed, he would be freed. He said: So I said to Nafi’: What is emphasis? He said: He repeats the oath in one thing."
"12478","(12478) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Hisham al-Distawai told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If the man says For a man who owes money: If you do not fulfill it on such-and-such a day, then he owes you alms, so it is not worth anything, even if he said: Even if not You give me until such and such day, and it is charity for the poor, so it is as he said."
"12479","(12479) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Mansour bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his mother, that she asked Aisha, may God be pleased with her, does not make a person’s statement: “All my wealth is in the way of God” or “in the crown of the Kaaba” atone, so she said: What expiates for it is what expiates an oath."
"12480","(12480) Abd al-Rahim and Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mis`ar, who said: I heard Hubayra speaking to al-Hakam ibn Utaiba since Thirty years. He said that one of our women made her house a gift, so Ibn Abbas ordered her to give her money."
"12481","(12481) Abd al-Rahim told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who brings his house to the House of God, he said: He sells it and sends its price to Mecca, or he goes and gives in charity. In Mecca, or he buys slaughtered animals and slaughters them in Mecca, and gives them in charity."
"12482","(12482) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who says to his kings: “He is a gift.” He said: “He is a gift of his value.”"
"12483","(12483) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali bin Atiq, about a man who guided his kingdoms and his kingdoms, he said Al-Shaabi: He will give their value, and Ata’ said: He will give a ram."
"12484","(12484) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, he said: I asked Ata’ about the man who said: He is the one who guides his servant. He said: He guides. A ram in its place."
"12485","(12485) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jami’ bin Abi Rashid, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who cleanses his house, he said: expiation for an oath."
"12486","(12486) Dawud bin Katheer Al-Jazari narrated to us, on the authority of Tariq bin Abi Murra, who said: I swore to my wife regarding a maid of hers that I I had sex with her and brought her to the House of God. So I had sex with her, so I asked Saeed bin Jubayr, and he said: Buy a body for its price. Then he slaughtered her."
"12487","(12487) Hamid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam; Concerning the man who gives the house, he said: He gives its value."
"12488","(12488) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Furat, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said, when he said of something:"
"12489","(12489) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, he said: When he said: He will guide one who travels from The pillars of the mosque, he will give them their value, or their price, and if he cannot find a gift, he will not give his money and make expiation. His right hand"
"12490","(12490) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, that it was desirable for a man to give something The thing is to move on."
"12491","(12491) Abu Amir Al-Aqdi narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qays, who said: I said to Saeed bin Al-Musayyab: I walk in this garment of mine. Until I take him to the Kaaba, if I speak to a friend of mine, he says: Do I regret it? I said yes, he said: Go and wear your dress, for the Kaaba is of no use to your dress and you, and say: Saeed commanded me, so I came. Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, and he said to me the same as what Saeed said. When I left him, his messenger approached me and said: Do you have any dirhams? I said: Yes, he said: Give it in charity, and say: Al-Qasim commanded me to do so with it."
"12492","(12492) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, about a man. He said: He guides The Euphrates and what it is called. He said: He guides what He possesses."
"12493","(12493) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It is expiation for an oath."
"12494","(12494) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, Ata’, and Mujahid. They said: He was not from Hadi to Let him buy a house with it and give it in charity."
"12495","(12495) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, he said: I asked Ata’ about seven dirhams that his wife sent him with. A guide to the House. Ata’ said: This house of yours is rich in your money, but give it to the poor among you. The body is the gifts of the house."
"12496","(12496) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, that a woman said: I was with Aisha, the Mother of the Believers. Then a woman brought her some jewelry and said: I brought this as a gift to the Kaaba, so Aisha said to her: If only I had given it to her. For the sake of God, and orphans and the needy, this house is given and spent on it from the wealth of God."
"12497","(12497) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Because I give my ring in charity. This is more beloved to me than being given a thousand gifts to the Kaaba."
"12498","(12498) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, he said: I heard him say: Because I would like to give in charity a dirham I would like to give a hundred thousand dirhams to the House, and if someone were to ask me for money, I would not give a dirham of it to the House."
"12499","(12499) Mahboub Al-Qawariri narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Habib, on the authority of Salem, who said: A man asked him about his gift. The Ka’bah, and he said: The Ka’bah is indispensable to your guidance. See a poor or needy person and feed him with broken pieces."
"12500","(12500) Muammar bin Sulaiman Al-Ruqqi narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, that he was not Fasting is divided into three days."
"12501","(12501) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I asked Abraham about fasting for three days in expiation. On the right, he said in our reading: {Fasting for three consecutive days}"
"12502","(12502) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: All fasting in the Qur’an is consecutive, except for making up for Ramadan."
"12503","(12503) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of al-Rabi’, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, he said: My father used to recite it: {Fasting for three consecutive days}"
"12504","(12504) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: In the Qur’an of Abdullah: {Fasting for three consecutive days}"
"12505","(12505) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say regarding fasting that expiates oaths: He fasts consecutively, and if he breaks his fast due to an excuse, he will make up one day in place of another day."
"12506","(12506) Hamid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid. They said: It was not Except Ramadan, nothing but successive."
"12507","(12507) Sharik bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: A man came to him. He said: I had intercourse with my wife while she was menstruating, so he said: Give half a dinar in charity. (Abu Dawud 270, Bayhaqi 316)"
"12508","(12508) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he raises it: He gives half in charity. dinar"
"12509","(12509) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Muqassam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He should give in charity a dinar, or half a dinar.

(Abu Dawud 268. An-Nasa’i 282)"
"12510","(12510) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, who said: A man came to Abu Bakr and said: I saw Sleeping as if I was urinating blood. He said: I see you coming to a woman while she is menstruating. He said: Yes. He said: Fear God, and do not repeat it."
"12511","(12511) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning a man who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, he said: He gives a dinar or half a dinar in charity."
"12512","(12512) Ibn Al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Ya’qub, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, he said: He seeks forgiveness God"
"12513","(12513) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, he said: He committed a sin, and he asks God for forgiveness from him."
"12514","(12514) Hushaym told us, saying: Ismail told us, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, similar to that."
"12515","(12515) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: He seeks forgiveness from God, he said: And Al-Hasan was seeing He is as he sees on appearances."
"12516","(12516) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: Whoever has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, We see on him the appearances."
"12517","(12517) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father; Concerning a man who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, he said: He apologizes and repents to God."
"12518","(12518) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Muthanna, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He seeks forgiveness from God."
"12519","(12519) Hushaym told us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla told us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: The man falls on His wife is menstruating. He said: He gives a dinar in charity."
"12520","(12520) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He is not obligated to do anything, but he does not repeat it."
"12521","(12521) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: A sin from which God seeks forgiveness."
"12522","(12522) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr al-Hubali, on the authority of Abu Hurri, that Omar asked Ali what she saw in a man Did he have intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating? He said: He does not have to make any expiation unless he repents."
"12523","(12523) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, regarding a man who swore not to maintain his relatives. He said: He will maintain his relatives. And he makes expiation for his oath. He said: Al-Sha’bi said: He maintains his ties of kinship, but he does not make expiation for his oath, even if I commanded him to make expiation. His right hand, I commanded him to fulfill what he said."
"12524","(12524) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir bin Nabatah that he heard him narrate, that two brothers were Two partners, and one of them wanted to separate from his brother, so he said: Every one of his slaves is free, or freed if he does not separate. His brother, and his mother had commanded him not to separate from his brother, so she asked Al-Hasan, or he was asked while he was hearing that, and he said: To make amends. He will take his oath and maintain his ties of kinship and share with his brother, or as he said: Abu Al-Alaa said many things: I narrated it to Al-Hakam bin He made it clear and said: This is the statement of Tawoos."
"12525","(12525) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abraham, about a man who swore not to speak to his father or brother Sharin. He said: He treats him kindly and enters upon him, but does not speak to him."
"12526","(12526) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who has intercourse with his wife while she is completing the month of Ramadan, they said: There is nothing wrong with him."
"12527","(12527) Umar ibn Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Maimoon, on the authority of Shuraih, that a man entrusted him with money and it was The Sultan was faced with that man because of his transgression, so he said to Shurayh: We ask you to swear to God. He said: I was paying for his wealth as much as I could, unless He was forced to turn right."
"12528","(12528) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who is asked by the ruler to swear that he will lead a Muslim man or his wealth, so he said: He must swear and declare disbelief. Right hand"
"12529","(12529) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of his father, He used to pronounce his oath with a strike rather than a strike, or with a strike less than a strike."
"12530","(12530) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Abu Ma’bad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Whoever swears an oath on the authority of He will strike us on his right hand, and his atonement is his abandonment, and for him there is one of the expiations, his good deeds."
"12531","(12531) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Qays bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, about a man He vowed to strike his servant with thirty lashes, or more. He said: He would collect them all and strike him once."
"12532","(12532) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim in Al-Mazhahir, he had prayers at the end of the night, Or the day, he said: It begins with fasting."
"12533","(12533) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Rabah, on the authority of Mujahid, regarding a man who swore to enter ihram. He said: He does not have to do anything."
"12534","(12534) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: expiation for an oath."
"12535","(12535) Marwan bin Muawiyah, on the authority of Hassan bin Abi Yahya, said: I heard Ikrimah and a man asked him, and he said: I I swore to my wife ten times that if I had intercourse with my maid of mine, he said: Ikrimah: If I had fulfilled her, it would have belonged to Satan. Go, for it is only an oath that will make you expiate."
"12536","(12536) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Jabir bin Zaid, who said: If he said: He is in ihram for Hajj and he blasphemes his oath."
"12537","(12537) Al-Muharbibi told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man. He said: He has to perform a thousand Hajj. He said: He has to perform expiation for the oath."
"12538","(12538) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who says: He is in ihram for a thousand Hajjs, and he performs Hajj as long as he is able."
"12539","Abdullah bin Muhammad told us, saying:

(12539) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He hated to say: And I will come to you, by God. Wherever he is, he said: God is in every place."
"12540","(12540) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, that Ibn Omar hated to hear a man say: No, by God. Wherever he is, he is in every place."
"12541","(12541) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zayd bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, that He hated to say: Your business will not come to you."
"12542","(12542) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zayd ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, he said: Do not say One of you swears by my father, my Lord, for he cannot be ransomed with anything."
"12543","(12543) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, regarding a man who vowed to hold his nose, said: It makes expiation for his oath."
"12544","(12544) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Jamraat al-Dab’iy, that a man from Banu Sulaym vowed to fight. He nodded and said: Ibn Abbas, a vow is two vows, so whatever is for God is fulfillment, and whatever is for Satan is atonement. Release your reins and straighten your right hand."
"12545","(12545) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, who said: I asked Jabir bin Zayd about a man who vowed to put Is your nose a gold ring? He said: He will continue to be a sinner as long as it continues, so let him make amends for his oath."
"12546","(12546) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Siwar, on the authority of al-Hasan; Concerning a man who holds his nose and performs Hajj on foot. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Likewise, remove this and perform Hajj riding and sacrifice your body."
"12547","(12547) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos? He said: No reins, no cuffs, and no wailing, meaning in Islam."
"12548","(12548) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar and Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Zuhr, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Ru`aniyi, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Malik, on the authority of Uqba ibn Amir al-Jihani, who said: My sister vowed to You walked barefoot to the House of God without khumra. So you asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Tell your sister to khumrah. And ride and fast for three days. (Bukhari 1866, Muslim 1264)"
"12549","(12549) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Humayd informed us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw May God bless him and grant him peace. A man was being guided between his two sons, and he said: What is this? They said: He vowed to walk to the House of God, and he said: God is free from this man torturing himself. Then he commanded him. So he rode (Bukhari 1865. Muslim 9)"
"12550","(12550) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Urwah ibn Adhinna, he said Ubayd Allah is his grandmother, and Malik said: His mother was made to walk, so she walked until she came to watering, then she was unable to do so. She walked, so she asked Ibn Umar, and he said: Marwa is to return the next year and walk from where she was unable."
"12551","(12551) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that he was asked about a man who vowed to He walked to the Kaaba, so he walked half the way and rode half of it. He said: Then Aamir said: Ibn Abbas said: He rides as long as he walks. And he walks as never before, and guides his body."
"12552","(12552) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, who said: Whoever said against him If he wants to walk, he can ride or guide him."
"12553","(12553) Abd al-Rahim and Abu Khaled al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali; Concerning a man who is made to walk to the House of God. Abdul Rahim said: He rides and sheds blood, and Abu Khaled said: He guides his body."
"12554","(12554) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed Al-Bajli, who said: I was under the pulpit of Ibn Al-Zubayr was on his way, then a man came and said: O Commander of the Faithful, I have vowed to perform Hajj on foot, even if that is the case. And so I walked, fearing that I would miss Hajj. I rode. He said: There is no fault on you. Come back a year ago and walk as long as you rode. And ride as long as you walk."
"12555","(12555) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who vowed to perform Hajj on foot, he said: He will walk, and if he is interrupted, he will ride and provide for his body."
"12556","(12556) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidy, who said: I heard Al-Qasim and he was asked about a man who swore that he would walk to... House, so he walked, and became tired, so he rode. He said: If he is coming, let him walk as long as he rode, and let him ride as long as he rode. He said: And I heard Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt says: He rides and guides his body."
"12557","(12557) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, about a man who was walking to the House. So he walks, then he becomes weary. He said: He rides, so if he is able, he rides as long as he walks, and walks as long as he rides."
"12558","(12558) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubaid Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Concerning a man who says that I must walk to the Kaaba. He said: This is a vow, so let him walk."
"12559","(12559) Hammad bin Khalid Al-Khayyat told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hilal, who heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab say: Whoever said, “I must walk.” To the House of God. There is nothing to do except to say: I have a vow to walk to the Kaaba."
"12560","(12560) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: A man from among us was appointed to walk to the house in Something, so Al-Qasim came and asked him about that, and he said: He will walk to the House."
"12561","(12561) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Yazid Abu Ibrahim al-Taymi, who said: If a man says: For God’s sake, or for a Hajj, it is the same, and if he says: A vow is for God’s sake, or for a Hajj, then it is the same."
"12562","(12562) Omar bin Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Zaid, who said: Two men came to Al-Qasim and asked him, and I was listening, on the authority of a man who made... He must walk to the House of God, he said: Al-Qasim said: Warn? He said: No. He said: Let his oath be expiated."
"12563","(12563) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar, may God be pleased with him, who said: I made a vow. During the pre-Islamic era, then I converted to Islam, so I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered me to fulfill my vow.

(Bukhari 2042. Abu Dawud 3318)"
"12564","(12564) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Every oath he swore to God in righteousness will be fulfilled in Islam."
"12565","(12565) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos regarding a man who vowed during the pre-Islamic era, then he converted to Islam. He said: He will fulfill it. With your vow"
"12566","(12566) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hudhali, that a woman vowed to light lamps in a sale while she was a Christian. So she converted to Islam and wanted to fulfill her vow. Al-Hasan and his followers said: You should light lamps in Muslim mosques, and Ibn Sirin said: Not. Something happened to her, so I presented their opinions to Al-Shaabi, and he said: The deaf person is right and your companions are wrong. Islam has destroyed what was. Before him"
"12567","(12567) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He forbade vows, and said: It does not bring good, but rather it is extracted from the miserly person. (Bukhari 6608, Muslim 2)"
"12568","(12568) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Beware of vows, for God does not bestow His blessings upon bribery, but rather it is something that is extracted from He is a miser. (Bukhari 6694, Abu Dawud 3281)"
"12569","(12569) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Huraira, he said: I will never make a vow."
"12570","(12570) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a Muslim kills a non-Muslim, he is not liable. Atonement"
"12571","(12571) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, regarding a Muslim who kills a non-Muslim by mistake. He said: Their expiation. Either way"
"12572","(12572) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: A group of people passed by The people of the Levant bought a slave girl and freed her. She threw a ton of cane on a boy and killed him. She was brought to her stolen, and he said: They searched for its guardians, but they did not find anyone. So he looked for a while and thought, and said: God said: {So whoever does not find one, then fast. Two consecutive months} Go and fast for two consecutive months, and they do not charge you anything."
"12573","(12573) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: A maid threw a ton of reeds on a boy and killed him. So Masruq was brought about that, and he said: Does he know of any of her friends? They said: We do not know who is her client. He said: Does she have any wealth? They said: She does not know how much money she has. He said: So she was told to fast for two consecutive months."
"12574","(12574) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Zakaria bin Abi Zaydi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Masruq was asked, On the authority of this verse: {And whoever kills a believer by mistake - the freedom of the slave of a believer will be freed, and his blood money will be delivered to his family} {So whoever does not find Fasting for two consecutive months}: He was asked about fasting for two months on behalf of a slave alone, or on behalf of blood money and slaves. He said: Whoever does not find it is free of blood money and slaves."
"12575","(12575) Marwan bin Muawiyah Al-Fazari told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman Al-Taifi, on the authority of Maimunah bint Kardam Al-Yasariyah, that his father met the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was his companion, so he asked him, and he said: I vowed to sacrifice Bawana, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Is there an idol in her? She said: My father said: No, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Then fulfill your vow where you vowed. (Abu Dawud 3302, Ahmad 6/366)"
"12576","(12576) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Habib al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, that a man He vowed to pray in the Holy House, so he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: May God bless him and grant him peace, pray here, meaning in the Sacred Mosque. So he repeated three times to him, and said: Pray wherever you said.

(Abu Dawud 3298, Ahmad 3/363)"
"12577","(12577) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: He was asked about a man who vowed to come to the Holy House, and he said: If He brought him back to the Sacred Mosque. He was most loyal."
"12578","(12578) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, about a man who vowed to perform Hajj. Al-Mada'in, he said: To atone for his oath, and not go to Al-Mada'in."
"12579","(12579) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, about a man who vowed to walk to Al-Rustaq. He said: He walks"
"12580","(12580) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, who said: Ata was asked about a man who made To pray such-and-such in the Mosque of Elijah in the Sacred Mosque, for it is That is sufficient, and prayer in the Sacred Mosque is better."
"12581","(12581) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a woman who vowed to come to a place she had named, He said: Let her see how much she has spent, then give it in charity, but do not go there."
"12582","(12582) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Marwan bin Mahan Al-Taymi, who said: I heard Al-Sha’bi and he was asked about a woman. She vowed to slaughter a cow. Should she sell its skin? He said: Yes, and Ibn Ash’u said: But I do not know that. Al-Shu’bi said: If I had said “meat”, there would be no harm in it. She only shed her blood, so she has shed her blood."
"12583","(12583) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, who said: My mother vowed that if she saw a hair on my face, she would slaughter his body, or He said: Hadiyya. He said: And the living ones were slaughtering cows. He said: So I came to Shurayh and asked him, and he settled the two of them."
"12584","(12584) Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who made a corpse for the poor, he said: He is rewarded with cows."
"12585","(12585) Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ma’abad, that he was with a woman from his family. She secluded herself in the mosque for a month, so she secluded herself for twenty-nine days, then she had her period, returned to her family, and then purified herself. Then her husband came to her and said: I came unharmed and Al-Qasim, and they said: Go to Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, then come to us. He said: So I went to Saeed and asked him, and he said: He betrayed one of the limits of God, and erred in the Sunnah, and she must resume it. He said: So I returned. To Al-Qasim and Salim, and I informed them of what he said, and they said: That is what we saw."
"12586","(12586) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If he has intercourse The person in seclusion annulled his itikaf and resumed it."
"12587","(12587) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Bukair ibn Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Mujahid in Al-Mu’tikaf When he has intercourse, he says: He gives two dinars in charity."
"12588","(12588) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who cheated on his wife while he was in seclusion: Indeed, in the same position as the one who cheated in Ramadan, the same is upon him as the one who cheated In Ramadan."
"12589","(12589) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He makes up for his i’tikaf."
"12590","(12590) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamiya ibn Marthad, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: They used to have intercourse while they were They were secluded, until it was revealed: {And do not associate with them while you are secluded in the mosques}"
"12591","(12591) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Whoever has sexual intercourse with his wife while he is in seclusion He is required to pay expiation, just like the one who falls ill during Ramadan."
"12592","(12592) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When the one who is in itikaf has intercourse, he should face."
"12593","(12593) Ibn Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, about a woman who vowed to seclude fifty people. One day, she secluded herself for forty days, then her husband came and sent for her, and she came to him. He said: Complete what remained."
"12594","(12594) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who has intercourse with his wife while he is in seclusion, he said: He is free, free."
"12595","(12595) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Everything in the Qur’an is: or or or faww. In it there is a choice, and everything in it: (So whoever does not find, then the one next to him, and if he does not find, then the one next to him)."
"12596","(12596) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Ikrimah similar to this."
"12597","(12597) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: What was in the Qur’an: or Or his companion has a choice."
"12598","(12598) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning two men who were killed completely, he said: They must both make atonements."
"12599","(12599) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him, he said: There is one expiation for them both."
"12600","(12600) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Shu’bi, he said: Don’t you see that if a people killed a man They participated in his killing, and each one of them was required to make an expiation."
"12601","(12601) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Shu’bi, he said: If a people had gathered together to kill a man, it would have been There is an expiation for each one of them, meaning a mistake. He said: The judge was of the view that this was the case."
"12602","(12602) Ibn Numayr, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a people kills a man, then everyone is responsible for it. Among them is liberation."
"12603","(12603) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Burd Abi Al-Ala’, on the authority of an alcoholic among the people They kill the man. He said: Every man among them must make an expiation, and the blood money must be paid on all of them."
"12604","(12604) Muhammad bin Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ubaid bin al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, who said: He was Aisha is a slave, or a woman who freed you from the descendants of Ismail. He said: He came as a captive from Yemen. Mas’ar said: I see him from Before, it is said to her: Khawlan. He said: Then he forbade her to be freed from them. He said: Then he brought a captive of Mudar. He showed him. He said: Who He built Al-Anbar, so he ordered her to free one of them."
"12605","(12605) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Abi Zayd, who said: Amer was asked about a man who made freed people from The son of Ishmael, if he entered the house of so-and-so, and he entered him, he said: There is no expiation for her. The man said: I cannot find them. He said: Then fast. Four consecutive months, two months for each slave, perhaps he might make amends for something."
"12606","(12606) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The time may be morning. And in the evening."
"12607","(12607) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of a man among them, who said: I asked Ibn Abbas, I said: I swore not to speak to him. A man of time, he said: Then Ibn Abbas recited: {Its food is given every time, by the permission of its Lord}, he said: time is a year."
"12608","(12608) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The time will be six months."
"12609","(12609) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The time will be six months."
"12610","(12610) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmala, who said: I heard Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab and a man asked him, and he said: I swore to my wife that she would not go in to her family for a while, and he said: “The time is not between the date palms sprouting until they bear fruit, and what between that it bear fruit until it bears fruit, so Sa`id said to him: {Allah gives an example of a word} to His saying: {It gives its fruit at all times. By the permission of her Lord}"
"12611","(12611) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who swore never to speak to a man for a while, and they said: Now is the Sunnah."
"12612","(12612) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: The time will be six months."
"12613","(12613) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, He said: The time is two months. Indeed, the palm tree feeds the entire year except two months."
"12614","(12614) Muawiyah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Al-Hunn Six months"
"12615","(12615) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Asim bin Shammikh, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, who said: Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, strove to take an oath, he would say: No, by the One in whose hand is the soul of Abul-Qasim.

(Abu Dawud 3259. Ahmad 3/48)"
"12616","(12616) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: It was the right The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is the one to which he swears: “No,” and He is the One who turns hearts. (Bukhari 7391, Abu Dawud 3258)"
"12617","(12617) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hilal, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Huraira, he said: It was The right hand of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: No, and I ask forgiveness from God. (Abu Dawud 3260, Ahmad 2/288)"
"12618","(12618) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, he said: I was He was sitting with Ibn Masoud above his house, when the sun had set, and Abdullah said: This is the one by whom there is no god but Him, when he broke his fast. The fasting person"
"12619","(12619) Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah, he said: It was Ali, may God be pleased with him, was giving a speech, and he said: No, by the one who separated the love and healed the soul."
"12620","(12620) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’dah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah says: No, by the Lord of this Kaaba."
"12621","(12621) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Ziyad al-Harithi, who said: A man said to Abu Hurairah: Are you the one who forbids fasting on Friday? He said: No, by God, this sanctuary, or this building."
"12622","(12622) Hafs and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd, on the authority of Abd God, He said: By Him there is no god but Him."
"12623","12623) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythama, on the authority of Masruq, that Aisha said about something that she swore Ali: No, by the one in whom the believers believe and the disbelievers disbelieve in him. (Ibn Saad 82)"
"12624","(12624) Muhammad bin Musab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Hilal bin Abi Maymunah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Rifa’a al-Janni, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, swore, He said: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad. (Ahmed 16)"
"12625","(12625) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Abu Al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Sa’id bin Jubair said: Ibn Abbas said: If Fa’a has committed blasphemy, and if he does not do so, then she is single and has more right to her soul."
"12626","(12626) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Harun bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jubayr, That Ziyad saw Abu Musa looking gloomy, so he said to him: What is the matter with you? So he mentioned that he had had intercourse with his wife, so he ordered him to make amends, so he did."
"12627","(12627) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Ash-Sha’athi, on the authority of Alqamiya, and the companions of Abdullah, they said: Concerning a man who has intercourse with his wife, then has intercourse with her before his oath has been fulfilled, he said: He expiates his oath."
"12628","(12628) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Ash-Sha’athi, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: If the master fails, he disbelieves."
"12629","(12629) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, who said: If a man has intercourse with his wife, then he fulfills his duty. Atonement"
"12630","(12630) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’iya, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that he did not consider it obligatory to pay expiation in His right hand"
"12631","(12631) Ibn Aliyah, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: Its water is an expiation."
"12632","(12632) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, regarding the one who is given the guardianship of his wife and he will be rewarded. He said: It was Some of them say: It is expiation."
"12633","(12633) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who swears that he will not have sexual intercourse with his wife for ten days, then he has sexual intercourse with her before the ten days, saying: There is no expiation for him."
"12634","(12634) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who made it obligatory to fast a month, he said: If he names a known month, let him fast from it and follow it, and if he does not name a known month, Or he did not intend, then let him fast for thirty days, and if he fasted upon the crescent, and broke his fast upon its sighting. So it was twenty-nine days, that is sufficient, and if he separates, then the days will come forward."
"12635","(12635) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalababi; Concerning a man who makes a month’s fast upon him, he said: He knows best what he has made, and He has made it his right hand."
"12636","(12636) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man imposes a month’s fast upon him, He did not name any of the months. He said: If he wants, he can continue, and if he wants, he can separate."
"12637","(12637) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of Maimun, who said: The vow to fast is consecutive."
"12638","(12638) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Ata, and someone who asked Abraham told me about a man who vowed to fast. Monthly, they said, “He fasts for thirty days,” meaning “separately.”"
"12639","(12639) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He did not see any harm in feeding a poor person. One ten times in expiation for swearing an oath."
"12640","(12640) It was narrated to us that Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: In expiation only an oath is sufficient. Feeding ten poor people."
"12641","(12641) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who does not find poor Muslims, so he gives to the Jews and Christians. Al-Sha’bi said: He will be sufficient, and the arbiter said: No. He will reward him, and Abraham said: I hope that if he does not find anyone else, he will reward him."
"12642","(12642) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he had twenty He disbelieved."
"12643","(12643) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin that they did not schedule anything in that matter."
"12644","(12644) Mu’tamar narrated to us, saying: I said to Mu’mar: A man swears an oath and does not have any food except what he expiates. He said: His followers used to say: He fasts for three days."
"12645","(12645) Affan told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; Concerning a man who swears an oath and has only three dirhams, so he swears an oath. He said: He is an infidel."
"12646","(12646) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Farqad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he had twenty dirhams He has to do expiation."
"12647","(12647) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of Farqad, on the authority of Ibrahim Like him"
"12648","(12648) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he used to say: If he swore on milk that he would not eat it. Butter, then it is from milk, and if he swears on butter then he should eat milk, and if he swears on meat then he should not eat lard, and if he swears on meat then he should not eat fat. On the fat, let him eat meat."
"12649","(12649) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: Our companions used to say: If he swears an oath on milk, he will not eat ghee. Nor of cheese, and if he swears on ghee and cheese, he will eat of milk."
"12650","(12650) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, he was asked about a man who said: To his wife. If he eats meat, then his wife. He was divorced and ate fish. He said: This is divorced. God Almighty said: {You shall eat fresh meat}"
"12651","(12651) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He broke his oath. God Almighty said: {You shall eat fresh meat}."
"12652","(12652) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Amer, who said: A man asked Ibn Abbas about a man who vowed to He slaughtered his son. He said: He slaughtered a hundred camels, just as Abdul-Muttalib ransomed his son for them. He said: And others said: A ram, as he ransomed. Abraham, his son Isaac. So I asked Masruq, and he said: This is one of the steps of Satan, and there is no expiation for it."
"12653","(12653) Abbad told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning a man who says: He is slaughtering his son. He said: A ram just as Abraham ransomed Isaac."
"12654","(12654) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa`id, on the authority of al-Qasim, who said: I was with Ibn Abbas, and I came to him. A woman, and she said: I have vowed to sacrifice my son. So he said: Ibn Abbas: Do not sacrifice your son and make expiation from your right hand. He said: A man said to Ibn Abbas: There is no fulfillment of a vow in the case of disobedience, so he said: Ibn Abbas: Didn’t he say: God is in the case of unjust people: {Indeed, they speak a disgraceful speech and a falsehood.} Then he said, “Indeed, of the infidels I have not heard.”"
"12655","(12655) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, regarding a man who vowed to sacrifice his son. He said: May God guide you."
"12656","(12656) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: When he said: He will slaughter his son, he said: Hajj"
"12657","(12657) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata’, who said: When he said: He will slaughter it. So we became"
"12658","(12658) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ikrimah, about a man who vowed to sacrifice His son, he said: He slaughters a ram and gives its meat in charity. Then he said: Indeed, there was for you in Abraham the most beautiful."
"12659","(12659) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abraham, regarding a man who vowed to sacrifice his son. He said: He will perform Hajj and slaughter his body."
"12660","(12660) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning a man who says: He is slaughtering his son. He said: He is offering his blood sacrifice, or a ram."
"12661","(12661) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Ghaffar Al-Muthanna bin Sa’id, who said: I asked Jabir bin Zaid, about a man, who said to a man He will guide you if your family is not pleased. He said: He will guide you as a ram."
"12662","(12662) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata’, who said: When he said: He will guide his son, So he smashed it."
"12663","(12663) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If he said: He will give his son, then a ram."
"12664","(12664) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When he said: He is giving a gift, barefoot and on foot, he said: He performs Hajj, and he walks barefoot, and does not ride, but carries the one he swore to."
"12665","(12665) Abd al-Rahim and Waki` told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali; Concerning a man saying to another man, “I will give you a gift,” and Waki’ said: He said to his son. He said: “I will give you my blood money.”"
"12666","(12666) Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He performs Hajj."
"12667","(12667) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He must perform Hajj."
"12668","(12668) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Uthman ibn Hadhir, on the authority of Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar, They said: He guides brave men."
"12669","(12669) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, on the authority of Masruq, who said: He guides A ram."
"12670","(12670) Abbad told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, who said: I asked Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin about a man who had intercourse with his wife. And he did not disbelieve and was negligent in that. They said: You will be prepared for it."
"12671","(12671) Al-Dahhak Ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, he said: If Al-Mazhar says: No A pilgrim to her will not be left alone until he is divorced or becomes an unbeliever."
"12672","(12672) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, regarding a woman who appointed a duty upon herself or vowed to pray. Fifty mosques, and to give alms from fifty houses, and to give alms to them. So he commanded her not to give alms, for it is a disobedience that expiates blasphemy. Turn to the right and pray in fifty mosques, because prayer is part of obedience to God."
"12673","(12673) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a woman who vowed to pray to each of the pillars of the Basra Mosque, he said: She should pray according to the number of her pillars. The mosque is in one place."
"12674","(12674) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Murra, he said: I entered the mosque I was telling myself to pray two rak'ahs at each cylinder, and a man was looking at me, but I did not notice him. When I sat down, I looked. Then, behold, Abdullah was sitting, and I came to him and sat next to him. Then, behold, the man who was looking at me was with him. He said: And he did not feel it. In my place, he said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, a man entered the mosque and began to pray two rak’ahs at each cylinder, and he said: If he had known that God at the cylinder would not change until he finished his prayer, he would have said: So I left the rest of what I wanted to pray."
"12675","(12675) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he freed the child of adultery and his mother."
"12676","(12676) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he freed a child of adultery and his mother."
"12677","(12677) Abu Asama, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: He saw no harm in freeing a child of illegitimate children."
"12678","(12678) Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father regarding the emancipation of a child of adultery. He said to him: He did not seek reward."
"12679","(12679) Asbat narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, who said: Ata’ was asked about freeing a child of adultery. Should he free him? He said: Yes, his emancipation is good."
"12680","(12680) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Hariz, on the authority of Maryam bint Abi Yazid, On the authority of Umm Nujaid, she asked Abu Imamah about the child of adultery that she should emancipate. He said: He is like a fake dirham, give him in charity."
"12681","(12681) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Thawr al-Shami, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Rahman bin Saad, who said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and said: I have two boys, one of them is of mature age and the other is young, and I want to free one of them. Which of them do you think should I be freed? He said: Look for the most expensive of them, and they found a son born of adultery with the most expensive, so he ordered them to do so."
"12682","(12682) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Free the most of them for their price."
"12683","(12683) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that she was asked, about the child of adultery, and she said: He does not bear the burden of any sin of his parents. {Do not bear the burden of another woman}"
"12684","(12684) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Issa Al-Kabbat narrated to us, saying: I heard Al-Sha’bi saying: The child of adultery is the best of the three, but this Something Ka'b said is the worst of the three."
"12685","(12685) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that Omar said: Because I wear two sandals for the sake of God. Is more beloved to me than freeing a child born of adultery."
"12686","(12686) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Aisha, she said, “To give three times in charity.” Nuwaiyat, or to be wielded with a whip for the sake of God is dearer to me than freeing the child of fornication."
"12687","(12687) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Al-Abbas freed some of his slaves during his illness, so Ibn Abbas returned one of them. Two of them thought that they were children of adultery."
"12688","(12688) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that Amr ibn al-Aas freed a slave of his during his illness, so Abd responded. Of Allah ibn Amr, six of them were thought to be the children of fornication."
"12689","(12689) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyya, on the authority of Ali, that he was forced to be emancipated. The child of adultery"
"12690","(12690) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Asq, who said: I was the slave of Omar, and he used to propose to him Islam. And he said: {There is no compulsion in religion}, so when he came, he freed him."
"12691","(12691) Sharik told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Amir, that Omar freed a Jew or a Christian."
"12692","(12692) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abraham, that Ali freed a Christian or a Jew."
"12693","(12693) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he freed a Christian boy of his who had been a slave to him. For some of his family, so he returned to her with an inheritance, so he freed him."
"12694","(12694) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz freed a servant of his. Christian"
"12695","(12695) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that he disliked being emancipated as a Christian."
"12696","(12696) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali ibn Ata’, on the authority of someone who heard Abu Hurairah say: Fasting is only in Expiation for swearing an oath upon one who does not find it."
"12697","(12697) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin, who said: If you find out, do not fast."
"12698","(12698) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Amer bin Musab, that Aisha refrained from Her brother after he died."
"12699","(12699) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, who said: Tawoos was asked about a woman who died and had to seclude herself in the mosque for a year. It is forbidden, and she has four sons, all of whom like to make up for it on her behalf. Tawus said: Seclude yourself, I will keep your four sons in the mosque. The forbidden for three months and fasting."
"12700","(12700) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Abd Allah bin Utbah, that A woman vowed to seclude herself for ten days, but she died and did not seclude herself. He said: Ibn Abbas: Abstain from your mother."
"12701","(12701) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It does not make up for itikaf when dead."
"12702","(12702) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Tawoos used to say regarding a vow for the dead: He fulfills it. I inherited it among them: If a man is obligated to fast for a Sunnah, if they wish, every person may fast for three months."
"12703","(12703) On the authority of Ibn Abi Adi, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he disliked for a man to eat the meat of his sacrifice. The poor in expiation for swearing an oath."
"12704","(12704) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When a man said to another man, “He will give his gift on the edge of He appointed him and said: He will perform Hajj and slaughter his body."
"12705","(12705) Jarir, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, he was asked about a woman who prepared everything she ate from something she made to her servant. He said: There is no need to sell it."
"12706","(12706) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who breaks his fast for several days in Ramadan, he said: He must make expiation every day."
"12707","(12707) Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: A man came The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You have perished, so he said: What destroyed you? He said: I had intercourse with my wife during Ramadan, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Free his slaves. He said: I cannot find them, so he said: Fast for two consecutive months. He said: I am not able. He said: Feed sixty poor people. He said: I cannot find it. He said: Sit. So he sat. While he was like that, a basket of dates was brought to him, and he said to him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Go and give it in charity. He said: O Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, there is no one among the people of the Prophet’s household that is more in need of it than we are. He said: He made you laugh. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, until his fangs were visible, then he said: Go and feed him to your children."
"12708","(12708) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Al-Sa’ib bin Abi Wada’i, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, He said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I broke my fast one day of Ramadan, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Give alms, ask God for forgiveness, and fast a day in its place."
"12709","(12709) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ibn al-Mutawus, on the authority of al-Mutawus, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever breaks his fast on a day of Ramadan without a concession has not Its reward is fasting for a lifetime. (Tirmidhi 723. Ibn Majah 1672)"
"12710","(12710) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Abdullah Al-Shakuri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, who said: Abdullah said: Whoever breaks his fast on a day of Ramadan intentionally, without travel or illness, will never make up for it, even if he fasts all the time. All of it"
"12711","(12711) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Omar bin Ali Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Arfaja, on the authority of Ali, who said: Whoever breaks his fast on the day of He did not make up Ramadan intentionally for the rest of his life."
"12712","(12712) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khalid, on the authority of Amir, regarding one who breaks the fast. One day of Ramadan deliberately, they said: He seeks forgiveness from God and repents to Him, and does not return and spend a day in his place."
"12713","(12713) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab; Concerning a man who intentionally breaks his fast one day in Ramadan, he said: He must fast for the month."
"12714","(12714) Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He must fast for three thousand days."
"12715","(12715) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, he said: Asim said: I asked Jabir bin Zayd Aba Al-Sha’atha’ and I said: I informed you about Whoever breaks the fast on a day of Ramadan, what does he have to do? He said: No, but let him fast a day in his place and do a good deed out of that."
"12716","(12716) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He repents, seeks forgiveness, and fasts for a day. His place"
"12717","(12717) Abdi told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Ali bin Hakim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, about a man who broke his fast. One day of Ramadan, he deliberately said: He asks God for forgiveness for that and repents to Him and performs one day in his place."
"12718","(12718) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Ali bin Hakim, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, who said: I said: For him: A man deliberately broke his fast on a day of Ramadan. What is his expiation? He said: I don't know what his expiation is, a sin he committed. He seeks forgiveness from God and makes up for it one day in his place."
"12719","(12719) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He will spend a day in his place and ask forgiveness from God."
"12720","(12720) Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jafar Bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Aisha, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He mentioned that he was burned, so he asked him about his situation, and he mentioned that he had intercourse with his wife during Ramadan, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace with a lump called arak, which contains dates. He said: Where is the burnt? So the man got up and said: Give this in charity."
"12721","(12721) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Salam bin Miskin, that he asked Jabir bin Zayd and Al-Hassan about a woman who was appointed As a gift, Jabir bin Zaid said: If she is well-off, then a cow, and if she is in difficulty, then a sheep, and Al-Hasan said: Atonement. On the right hand, you fast for three days."
"12722","(12722) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said: Concerning a man who says, “I owe a sacrifice,” or “I owe a vow,” he said, “Yameen.”"
"12723","(12723) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Salama Abi Bishr, on the authority of Ikrimah; Concerning a man who swears by his body and his gift, he said: From the steps of Satan."
"12724","(12724) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Qais ibn Saad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, about a man Ali Hadi said: No less than a sheep."
"12725","(12725) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, they said, when he said: Ali Hadi, and he did not name it. Something they said: Right."
"12726","(12726) Abdul-Wahhab narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: If he says, “Ali is a Hadi,” and does not name the name, then he may give him whatever he wants, even if Kabbah of ghazal."
"12727","(12727) Muhammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala’, on the authority of his followers, who said: A smart woman came and said: I vowed to seclude myself in the mosque, but the Sultan prevented me. He said: Make atonement for your oath."
"12728","(12728) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr bin Haram, who said: Jabir bin Zayd was asked about a woman. She was required to seclude herself for a month in the Grand Mosque, but an order was asked of her that she could not appear. He said: She secluded herself in a mosque. Believe in Him"
"12729","(12729) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who swears an oath of divorce and swears it. He said: The oath is based on what the one who swears it swears, and it is not the intention of the swearer. With something"
"12730","(12730) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whoever swears an oath to a man will see that it is not an oath. So, it is an oath that is determined."
"12731","(12731) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The oath is upon me. The intention of the one who swore."
"12732","(12732) Zaid told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Abbad bin Abi Salih told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The oath is based on the intention of the one who swears oath. (Muslim 22. Abu Dawud 3250)"
"12733","(12733) Zaid narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma’shar narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Faghawa’i, he said: Omar said, Your oath is based on what your companion has spoken true to you."
"12734","(12734) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he is oppressed, let him To make you leave with an oath, but if he is an unjust, then he has no right to make you leave you with an oath."
"12735","(12735) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When he says: I did not swear, he says: Oath. He makes her an unbeliever."
"12736","(12736) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: Abraham was among the eminent people, so he was asked about A man who was required to walk towards the Kaaba when he entered upon his son, and his companions bore him and brought him in. Then Abraham said, “With his hand.” They carried him and brought him in, so that he might walk."
"12737","(12737) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Saad bin Ubadah asked for a fatwa. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a vow to his mother. She died before she could fulfill it, so he said: Fulfill it on her behalf."
"12738","(12738) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Bunani, on the authority of Maimun, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, he was asked On the authority of a man who died with a vow, and he said: He may fast on his behalf as a vow."
"12739","(12739) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said on the authority of Ibn Abbas: If he dies with a vow, his guardian fulfills it on his behalf."
"12740","(12740) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abraham, regarding a man who died with a vow of fasting, he said: He feeds on it."
"12741","(12741) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who vowed to fast, but he died before he could fast. He said: It was astonishing for him to complete a fast for him."
"12742","(12742) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Tawoos, regarding a vow for the dead. He said: His heirs shall settle it among themselves. If a man is obligated to fast for a year, if he wishes, every person among them may fast for three months."
"12743","(12743) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Kurayb, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of them, on the authority of Sinan bin Abdullah al-Janni, that her paternal aunt told him that she came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, She said: O Messenger of God, my mother died and she had to make a vow to walk to the Kaaba, so he said: Are you able to walk? About us? She said: Yes, so he said: So walk on behalf of your mother. She said: Will that suffice on her behalf? He said: Yes, what do you think if she had a debt and paid it off, would it be accepted from you? She said: Yes, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God has more right to that. (Bukhari 2336)"
"12744","(12744) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Ata, on the authority of Ibn Buraida, on the authority of his father, who said: I was sitting at The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a woman came to him and said: My mother was required to fast for two months. Will that be rewarded for her? Should we fast on her behalf? He said: Yes."
"12745","(12745) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Malik, who said: The oath that does not expiate: the man swears A man has the property of a Muslim man, and he cuts it off unjustly, while he is lying about it."
"12746","(12746) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, Muhammad, and Al-Hasan in his saying: {Indeed, those who buy With the covenant of God and their oaths for a small price. They said: This is a man who seizes a man’s wealth with his oath."
"12747","(12747) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of al-Hasan, and Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Ma`ashar, On the authority of Abraham, they said: If he appears from it, but does not enter it; If I cheated on you, there is no limit to that and there is no time limit, if her cheating is expiated."
"12748","(12748) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Kurayb, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard him while he was with him. Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, Abdullah bin Shaddad bin Al-Haad, and Nafi’ bin Jubayr, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: There are three in which there is no oath: A child has no oath upon his parent, nor a woman has an oath upon her husband, nor a servant has an oath upon him. Her master"
"12749","(12749) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Layya, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Imran, he said: I asked Al-Qasim and Salim, about A man who appeared after his death and found nothing to free him from. Should he free her? They said: Yes."
"12750","(12750) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak in Dhahar from slaves if he did not find anything to free, He was not able to fast, so he wanted to marry her. He made her emancipation his dowry, so her emancipation was an expiation for zihaar, and she was His wife"
"12751","(12751) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mughirah; Concerning a man who frees from his female slave, he said: His reward is that he frees her."
"12752","(12752) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos; Concerning a man who separates himself from his child’s mother and does not find anything to expiate. He said: He frees her, and her emancipation will be an expiation. To the right hand"
"12753","(12753) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, and Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who enters into ihram when he is angry. He said: From the inclinations of Satan, he feeds ten poor people, even if it is in obedience to God. philif."
"12754","(12754) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he freed a slave Then he took something from the ground and said: I have no reward like this. I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever slaps a servant of his, then his expiation is his emancipation. (Ahmad 25. Muslim 1279)"
"12755","(12755) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yassaf, who said: An old man hastened and slapped a servant of his, so he said: Suwayd bin Muqrin: Is it impossible for you to do anything but have a free face? You have seen me seventy of Banu Muqrin. We have no servant except one. The youngest of us smote her. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Abu Dawud 5123, Muslim 33)"
"12756","(12756) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Bashar ibn Kadam al-Sulami, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Swearing is an oath, or one of regret. (Bukhari 1930, Ibn Hibban 4356)"
"12757","(12757) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Muhammad, on the authority of his father, who said: Omar said: Oathing is a sin, or I regret it"
"12758","(12758) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Abu Awany, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid; Concerning a man who says, “The wrath of God is upon me,” he said, “There is no expiation for him,” but it is more severe than that."
"12759","(12759) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man who says: God cut off my back, God cut off my core. He said: There is nothing wrong with him."
"12760","(12760) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: He makes infidels."
"12761","(12761) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: It makes expiation."
"12762","(12762) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who has intercourse with his wife and eats during Ramadan in one day, he said: One expiation will set one free."
"12763","(12763) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Al-Mazhar makes expiation. Even if he is righteous"
"12764","(12764) Al-Dahhak narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If Al-Mazhar is virtuous, he will not be considered an infidel, and he said: Al-Dahhak: And with him. We say"
"12765","(12765) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Aslam, the client of Anbasa, that he said: I asked Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab about a woman who swore no She was drinking her husband’s milk from a goat, so she drank. He said: She is not required to do anything, there is no right in food or drink."
"12766","(12766) Ja`far narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, he said: There was a man who had a goat, so he swore not to drink of its milk. When his wife saw that, she swore not to drink of its milk. They milked it, so they dried up the goats and lost them, so Abdullah came and mentioned that to him, and he said: It was only from Satan that they returned. To the best of what you used to do and drink."
"12767","(12767) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A man from the Ansar had a guest. So he delayed leaving his family, and said: You entertained my guest with dinner. They said: No. He said: No, by God, I will not feed him with your dinner tonight. His wife: Then, by God, I will not feed him. He said: Then the guest said: And I, by God, will not feed him either. He said: So he said: My guest is staying. Without food, bring your food and eat with it. When morning came, he went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him. With that, he said: I obeyed God and disobeyed Satan."
"12768","(12768) Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, Ali bin Hakim narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Al-Kharit, on the authority of Ikrimah, said: I have never given a fatwa with my opinion on anything other than this. A woman who had vowed to circumambulate asked me. The house was on four pillars, so I said to her: Perform tawaf for each pillar seven times."
"12769","(12769) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: I heard Ata’ and he was asked about a woman who swore to emancipate Her maid was not to speak to her neighbour for four years, and her maid died, and she loved to speak to her neighbour. He said: “Speak to her.” He gave something in charity, and said: Ibn Abi Mulika: I do not see any perjury in her."
"12770","(12770) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man who says: God threw me into Hell. He says: He declares disbelief."
"12771","(12771) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Tawus, who said: He does not disbelieve."
"12772","(12772) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir; Concerning a man who swears that he will not eat this food and sells it. He said: He eats its price and buys it with it."
"12773","(12773) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He neither sells nor buys it. There is food in it, so eat it."
"12774","(12774) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Salim ibn Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Sharhabeel ibn Al-Samat, he said: We said to Ka’b bin Murah: O Ka’b bin Murah, tell us on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and beware, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever frees a Muslim man will be redeemed from the Fire. He will be rewarded with every bone. A bone of it, and whoever frees two Muslim women who had redeemed him from the Fire, he will be recompensed with two bones, one of them From him (Nasa’i 2881, Ahmad 4/235)"
"12775","(12775) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Omar bin Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Saeed bin Murjaniya, he said: I heard him narrating on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Whoever frees the slave of a believer, God will free every part of him, a part of the Fire, until he frees his private parts. With joy

(Bukhari 2517, Muslim 1147)"
"12776","(12776) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Al-Hakam bin Abdul-Rahman Ibn Abi Na’am narrated to us, saying: You narrated to me. Fatima bint Ali said: He said: My father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever frees a Muslim or a believer. May God protect every part of Him from the Fire. (Nasa’i 4877)"
"12777","(12777) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Salih bin Hayy, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever has a female slave, disciplines her well, and teaches her well. Teach her, then free her and marry her, and he will have two rewards. (Bukhari 2544, Abu Dawud 2046)"
"12778","(12778) Abdou told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a woman who vowed to seclude herself for two months, so she decided to stop it. He said: If she completes the waiting period, that will be sufficient for her."
"12779","(12779) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Amr bin Abdullah Al-Ansari, that a man vowed to He slaughtered a body, so Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ali came and said: The body of a camel, and do not slaughter it except in Mecca, unless he intends to slaughter it. So wherever he intended, if he did not find it, then seven sheep. He said: I asked Salim and he said something like that.

He said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and he said: Like that, except that he said: If he does not find it, then ten of the sheep. He said: And I asked Ibn Zayd left and told him what the people said, so he said: I did not find our companions counting it except seven sheep."
"12780","(12780) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar Sulaiman bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Qays, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abd God, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Continue Hajj and Umrah, for they remove poverty and sins. Just as kayr removes the impurity of iron, gold and silver, there is no reward for an accepted Hajj except for heaven.

(Tirmidhi 810, Ahmad 1/387)"
"12781","(12781) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Omar He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Continue Hajj and Umrah, for they eliminate poverty and sins as well. The furnace removes impurities from iron. (Ibn Majah 2887. Ahmed 1/25)"
"12782","(12782) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Sumayyah, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: One life’s journey to another is atonement for what came between them, and the accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise.

(Bukhari 1773, Muslim 983)"
"12783","(12783) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar and Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever performs Hajj and does not commit obscenity and does not commit immorality, will return as his mother gave birth to him.

(Bukhari 1820 and Tirmidhi 811)"
"12784","(12784) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha; A sheikh told him about this mosque: Omar addressed them at the Gate of the Kaaba and said: No one will come to this house. Prayer therein until he touches the stone, unless what he did before that will be expiated for him."
"12785","(12785) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of a sheikh, who said, Omar bin Al-Khattab said: Whoever performs Hajj This house does not want anyone else. It has emerged from its sins like the day its mother gave birth to it."
"12786","(12786) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Salih, who said: A migrant woman was performing Hajj. When she returns, she passes by Omar, and he says to her: Did you dig? She says: Yes, and he says to her: Continue the work."
"12787","(12787) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: While Omar was sitting at the house, he came There were men from Iraq who were pilgrims, and they circumambulated the Kaaba and performed sa'wā between al-Safa and al-Marwah. Then Umar called them and said: I will defeat you to God. Other than him? They said: No, so he said: Did you dig? They said: Yes, so he said: Did you manage? They said: Yes, he said: Either, no, so they resumed work."
"12788","(12788) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Habib; Some people passed by Abu Dharr in Al-Rabdha, and he said to them: What is the matter with you but Hajj? They resumed work."
"12789","(12789) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; Ibn Masoud said that to some people."
"12790","(12790) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hussein, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: He saw a group of Hajj, and he said: Why?? These people know what will happen to them after forgiveness, and their eyes will be glorified."
"12791","(12791) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Habib bin Al-Zubayr, who said: I said to Ata’: I have informed you that the Messenger of God prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Do you perform your duties after Hajj? He said: No, but Othman and Abu Dharr."
"12792","(12792) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Damra, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: When the Hajj, Umrah performer, and Ghazi say takbeer, the one who follows him says takbeer, then the one who follows him, then the one who follows him, until It cuts off on the horizon."
"12793","(12793) Zayd ibn Harun told us, saying: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, on the authority of Mirdas ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Laythi, he said: We went to Abdullah bin Amr and he spoke to us. He said: There is no one who performs the ihram except that God says to him: Good news. Then Mardas said: O father. Muhammad, by God, God only gives good tidings of heaven. He said: Who are you, my nephew? He said: I am Mirdas. He said: Our choice was followed one by one."
"12794","(12794) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Asama bin Sa’id, on the authority of Musa bin Sa’d, who said: Omar said: Meet the pilgrims. And the Ammar, and the invaders, let them pray for you before they become defiled."
"12795","(12795) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Damra al-Saluluy, on the authority of Kaab, he said: The Hajj, the Umrah pilgrim, and the Mujahid in the path of God are the delegation of God. They asked, and they were given, and they supplicated, and they were answered."
"12796","(12796) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ali; Al-Hussein bin Ali met a people who were pilgrims, and they said: We want Mecca. He said: You are from the delegation of God, so when you come to Mecca So gather your needs and ask God for them."
"12797","(12797) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, who said: We used to meet Hajj. In Al-Qadisiyah, so we shake hands with them before they touch each other."
"12798","(12798) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Aisha bin Talha, on the authority of Aisha,

 She said: I said, O Messenger of God, is there a duty against women? He said: Yes, jihad in which there is no fighting: Hajj and Umrah.

(Bukhari 2875. Ahmad 6/165)"
"12799","(12799) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Hajj is the jihad of every weak person. (Ahmad 6/303, Tayalisi 1599)"
"12800","(12800) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Omar said: The Hajj will be forgiven, and whoever asks forgiveness for him. The Hajj, the rest of Dhul-Hijjah, Muharram, Safar, and the ten days of Rabi’ al-Awwal."
"12801","(12801) Sharik told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Mujahid; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O God, forgive the pilgrim, and those for whom the pilgrim asks forgiveness. (Hakim 441)"
"12802","(12802) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalab; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The pilgrim is the delegation of God, and the pilgrim is the delegation of his family. (Ibn Majah 2893; Ibn Hibban 4613)"
"12803","(12803) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Spending in Hajj is like spending in the way of God, a dirham for seven hundred dirhams. (Ahmad 5/354)"
"12804","(12804) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi’a, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Continue Hajj and Umrah, for they remove sins and poverty, just as The furnace removes impurities from iron. (Ahmad 1/25)"
"12805","(12805) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Suqi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: No one has come to this house seeking He is in need of religion or the world, unless he returns with his need."
"12806","(12806) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: Whoever circumambulates the Kaaba will neither raise one foot nor lower one’s feet. Otherwise, except that good deeds were recorded for him, and sins were erased from him, and status was raised for him, and I heard him. He says: Whoever counts a week, it will be like the straightness of his neck. (Tirmidhi 959. Ahmad 2/95)"
"12807","(12807) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Harith bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Mundakir, on the authority of his father, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever circumambulates the Kaaba for a week and does not utter it, it is like freeing a slave.

(Tabarani 845. Hakim 457)"
"12808","(12808) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman Al-Rawasi told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul Allah bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: Whoever circumambulates the Kaaba for fifty weeks will be free of sins. Like the day his mother gave birth to him."
"12809","(12809) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: Whoever circumambulates He stayed at home for a week, and prayed two rak’ahs. It was like the day his mother gave birth to him."
"12810","(12810) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: Whoever circumambulates the Kaaba He was like a straight neck."
"12811","(12811) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, on the authority of a man who named him. He said: Abu Sa`id said: Is it more beloved to me to circumambulate the Kaaba? Since he freed Taman."
"12812","(12812) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Suleiman, on the authority of a servant of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Sa’id ; Like the hadith of Abu Muawiyah."
"12813","(12813) Ibn Mahdi said, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Tawaf, or tawaf is better than Umrah after Hajj."
"12814","(12814) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Ibn Amir entered ihram from Khorasan."
"12815","(12815) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn al-Aas, He said: I performed Hajj once, and I agreed with Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas, so he entered ihram from Al-Munjashaniyah, and he is near Al-Basra."
"12816","(12816) Azhar Al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: We went out to Mecca and with us was Hamid bin Abdul Rahman. So we were deprived of the dwellings."
"12817","(12817) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Muslim bin Yassar entered into ihram for a domestic animal."
"12818","(12818) Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Imran bin Al-Husayn was deprived of sight."
"12819","(12819) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He was in ihram from the Holy House."
"12820","(12820) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Suqi, on the authority of a man he did not name; That Abu Masoud entered ihram from among the armed men."
"12821","(12821) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to love for a man the first time he performed Hajj to perform ihram. Home"
"12822","(12822) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr Al-Fuqaimi, on the authority of Hamza Al-Qurashi, on the authority of His father; Ibn Abbas entered ihram from the Levant during severe cold."
"12823","(12823) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hilal ibn Khabab, on the authority of his father, who said: I went out with Sa’id ibn Jubayr. Ihram from Kufa."
"12824","(12824) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythami, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Qays, who said: I went out among a group of The companions of Abdullah, we wanted Mecca. When we left the houses, prayer came. They prayed two rak’ahs, then they performed the ihram, and I performed the ihram. I did not want to be with them, but I hated disagreement."
"12825","(12825) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Black people were forbidden from Home"
"12826","(12826) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Atiyya, who said: Tell me who saw Qais bin Abbad enter ihram from Mirbad. Insight"
"12827","(12827) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When Alqamiya went out as a pilgrim, he would enter ihram from Najaf. He shortened his prayers, and the black man was entering ihram from Al-Qadisiyah."
"12828","(12828) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Juwayriyah, who said: I saw the lions in ihram than Bagmiri. A village from the villages of blackness."
"12829","(12829) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, who said: I saw that black ones were more ihram than kufi ones."
"12830","(12830) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Amara bin Zazan, on the authority of Makhul al-Azdi, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: A man is deprived of Samarkand, and from Basra, and from Kufa, and he said: I wish we could escape the time that has been appointed for us."
"12831","(12831) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, who said: I went out with Al-Qasim, and he entered into ihram from Al-Rabadhi."
"12832","(12832) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila; Ali was in ihram from Medina."
"12833","(12833) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’tha’i, he said: I saw Al-Harith bin Suwayd. Al-Taymi and Amr bin Maymun entered ihram from Kufa."
"12834","(12834) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’bā narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah; Ali was asked about the words of God Almighty: (And complete the Hajj and the Umrah for the sake of God.) He said: To enter ihram for the part of your family."
"12835","(12835) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, on the authority of Tawus, who said: They are completed on their own, with two continuations. Who is your family?"
"12836","(12836) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Hamza Al-Qurashi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He entered ihram from the Levant during a severe winter."
"12837","(12837) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Suhaim, on the authority of Umm Hakim bint Umayya, on the authority of Umm Salamah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever dedicates his life to the Holy House, he will be forgiven.

(Abu Dawud 1738. Ahmad 6/299)"
"12838","(12838) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Ibn Amir entered into ihram from Khurasan, so Uthman bin Affan and others criticized him and hated him."
"12839","(12839) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymiy, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: Enjoy your clothes, for your robes are of no avail to you from God at all."
"12840","(12840) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Alqamiya used to enjoy Her clothes"
"12841","(12841) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of a sheikh called: Muslim; Omar saw a man who had entered ihram from Qatar in bad condition, and he said: Look at what this man has done to himself, and he was pleased with it. May God bless him."
"12842","(12842) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Imran bin Husayn was deprived of sight, so he came to Omar, and he was harsh to him and said: People say that a man from among the companions of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered ihram from among the countries of Egypt."
"12843","(12843) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Muslim Abi Salman; A man entered ihram from the Kufa, and Omar saw him in bad shape, so he took it by the hand and started circling it around his throat, and said: Look at what this man did with himself, and God has generously extended it to him."
"12844","(12844) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Miskin Abu Hurairah narrated to us, saying: I heard Mujahid and a man asked him: Which of them? Would I rather enter into ihram from my home, or from my people’s mosque, or from an Egyptian mosque, or from the time? Mujahid said: I enter ihram on the day of Tarwiyah, so I fear that I will not be permitted until I complete my ihram."
"12845","(12845) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If he imitates the hadith, and his companion wants Umrah, or Hajj, he has entered ihram."
"12846","(12846) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he imitates the hadith, and his companion wants to enter ihram, It is obligatory to enter ihram."
"12847","(12847) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: I saw a man in Al-Qadisiyah who had imitated his gift. He was wearing a cloak and a turban, so I ordered him to remove his turban, and he said: If a man imitates, or embellishes, then he has entered ihram."
"12848","(12848) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’tha’i, who said: If he imitates the Hajj, he enters ihram."
"12849","(12849) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’ and Ibn Al-Aswad, who said: He is not permitted to imitate it, nor to deprive it. Unless He wills for a day, or two days."
"12850","(12850) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: He saw a man who had imitated him, so he said: As for this man, he has entered into ihram."
"12851","(12851) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, and Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Whoever glorifies, or imitates, it is obligatory He must enter ihram."
"12852","(12852) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever imitates, or glorifies, Or he has hair, then he has entered ihram."
"12853","(12853) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and Suleiman bin Yasar, who said: Saad ibn Qays went out, and when he was wearing a cloak and his wife was walking towards him, he saw that his body had been trimmed, so he removed it. His head is from the hand of a woman, and he said: Whoever trims this body has completed his ihram."
"12854","(12854) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid, they said: When he imitates his guidance, or exalts him, he He wants to enter ihram, so he has entered ihram."
"12855","(12855) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Maimun ibn Abi Shabib, who said: If he imitates, or Jalla, or Ash'ar, has declared ihram."
"12856","(12856) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about a man who feels Hadi? He said: If he feels the sacrifice and performs it during the months of Hajj, then Hajj is obligatory for him, and if he does that in other months of Hajj then it is not It is obligatory for him."
"12857","(12857) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Hammad about a man who imitates his body? He said: If he wishes, he will not enter ihram."
"12858","(12858) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Whoever imitates has declared ihram."
"12859","(12859) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I used to The necklaces are for the guidance of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he imitates his guidance, then he sends it, then he performs it, no He avoids something that is forbidden. (Bukhari 1702. Muslim 365)"
"12860","(12860) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas; He was sent with guidance, and then he would not abstain from anything of what the Muhrim used to abstain from."
"12861","(12861) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Whoever is sent to guide him, he will not He abstains from anything that a muhrim abstains from, except for the night of the night, in which case he abstains from women."
"12862","(12862) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to issue a fatwa about that, and say: He should not abstain from anything that a person in ihram abstains from."
"12863","(12863) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He who Welcome, and whoever meets you."
"12864","(12864) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: He sent with me Abdullah With his gift, but he was not deprived of it."
"12865","(12865) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah; He was sent with guidance, and he would not withhold what the Muhrim refrained from."
"12866","(12866) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father; Omar, Ali, and Ibn Abbas used to say about a man who sends with his body: He withholds what he withholds from. Ihram, not that he does not recite the Talbiyah. Ja`far said: He will meet with them one day, so if that day is the one he will meet with them To feel, abstain from what a mahram abstains from."
"12867","(12867) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’; When Ibn Umar was sent with a gift, he would abstain from doing what the mahram abstained from, without saying the Talbiyah."
"12868","(12868) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, who said: Muhammad bin Ibrahim informed me that Rabi’ah bin Abd God Ibn Al-Hadeer told him: He saw Ibn Abbas, who was the governor of Basra, during the time of Ali bin Abi Talib, sitting on the pulpit of Basra, So he asked people about him? They said: He commanded his brother to be imitated, so he stripped himself of it. So I met Ibn al-Zubayr, and I mentioned that to him, and he said: An heresy. By the Lord of the Kaaba."
"12869","(12869) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: If a man is sent with a gift, the one who He will send him with him to imitate such-and-such on such-and-such day from that day, then he will abstain from some of the things he abstained from. Narrated by Muharram"
"12870","(12870) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Mu’adh, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Life is permissible for eternity, except Three days; The Day of Sacrifice, and two days of the days of Tashreeq."
"12871","(12871) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos; He was asked about Umrah? He said: When the days of Tashreeq have passed, then perform Umrah whenever you wish until next time."
"12872","(12872) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Ali said: In every month there is a lifetime. Saeed bin Jubair said: In every year of life there is a life."
"12873","(12873) Abbad told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Perform Umrah as long as the razor enables you."
"12874","(12874) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Husayn, on the authority of some of the descendants of Anas ibn Malik, who said: Anas ibn Malik performs Umrah here in Mecca, and whenever he bathes his head, he goes out and performs Umrah."
"12875","(12875) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He used to perform Umrah every year of his life, except for the year of fighting, in which case he performed Umrah in Shawwal and Rajab."
"12876","(12876) Azhar Al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: He did not see the Umrah except once in the year."
"12877","(12877) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Sadiqa, on the authority of Al-Qasim; He hated to perform Umrah twice every month."
"12878","(12878) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They did not perform Umrah during the Sunnah, except bitterly"
"12879","(12879) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Ata’ about the Umrah twice in the month? He said: No problem."
"12880","(12880) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, who said: Al-Hasan did not see ‘Umrah except in every year."
"12881","(12881) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Ibn Abbas saw a man cursing. His wife, and he said: What's the matter with you? He said: I have died, or I have wished, so Ibn Abbas said: Do not curse her, and shed blood for that."
"12882","(12882) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Aban bin Taghlib, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: A man from the people of Taif came in ihram for Hajj, and he saw They met women in an orchard, so he continued looking at them until he was gone, so he asked Saeed bin Jubair? He said: Spill some blood and complete your Hajj."
"12883","(12883) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Hubayra al-Dhabi, who said: I went out to Mecca with my wife. So I told her, and I was upset, so I asked Ata? He said: Shaa."
"12884","(12884) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Hajj is not invalidated until the two circumcisions meet, then If two circumcisions meet, the Hajj is invalidated and a fine is required."
"12885","(12885) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Zaid bin Jubayr, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Umar, when a woman came to him. She said: I vowed to perform Hajj, but I had never performed Hajj before this Hajj? He said: This is the Hajj of Islam, so seek what you fulfilled your vow with."
"12886","(12886) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Wasil, the client of Abi Uyaynah, who said: A sheikh who heard Ibn Abbas narrated to me, A woman came to him and said: I vowed to perform Hajj, but I did not perform the Islamic Hajj. So Ibn Abbas said: I have fulfilled them, by God. The Kaaba"
"12887","(12887) Abdul Wahhab told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah; That a man vowed to perform Hajj, but did not perform it. He said: The obligatory prayer and the vow are sufficient for him."
"12888","(12888) Al-Muharbibi told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; Concerning a man who had an oath during Hajj, and he did not perform the Hajj of Islam, so Hajj was made easy for him. He said: It suffices for both of them. If he is able to do something, let him perform Hajj."
"12889","(12889) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr (h) and on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid They said: The Hajj of Islam suffices for your Hajj and your vow."
"12890","(12890) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A man said to him: I had a vow to perform Hajj, but I did not perform Hajj. Hajj al-Islam, so which one should I start with? He said: Start with the Hajj of Islam."
"12891","(12891) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Abu Sulaiman, who said: I heard Anas say about a man who vowed to perform Hajj, He did not perform the Hajj of Islam. He said: It begins with the obligatory Hajj."
"12892","(12892) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered into ihram after the prayer."
"12893","(12893) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered ihram after the noon prayer, and Al-Hasan liked to enter ihram after the noon prayer. If he does not do that, then after the afternoon prayer."
"12894","(12894) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, who said: Your predecessors used to prefer reciting the Talbiyah on four days. placements; At the end of prayer, when they descend into a valley or at its height, and when the companions join."
"12895","(12895) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is recommended to recite the Talbiyah in places; At the end of the prescribed prayer, and when you ascend a high place, and when you descend a valley, and whenever your camel reaches you, standing, and whenever you I found companionship."
"12896","(12896) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father; He was in ihram after the obligatory prayer."
"12897","(12897) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Khaythamiyah, who said: They used to like to recite the Talbiyah at six times; He came back to prayer, and when he rode a man on his mount, and when he ascended, he ascended, and when he descended in a valley, and when he met one another Some"
"12898","(12898) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, who said: I asked Ata’ about the Talbiyah, if a man wants to enter ihram? He said: If you wish, then at the end of the prayer, and if you wish, then when the camel is sent for you, you will start while you are riding, and say: {Glory be to Him. He subjugated this to us, and we would not be able to abide by it."
"12899","(12899) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Hayyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’atha’i, Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: If some of them were to enter ihram while he was riding, and if some of them were to enter ihram while he was eating."
"12900","(12900) Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, on the authority of Aflah, who said: Al-Qasim used to perform the prayer after every prayer. Voluntary and obligatory."
"12901","(12901) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; In a state of ihram, his fingernail is broken. He said: If it hurts you, throw it away."
"12902","(12902) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, who said: If it is a splinter, then he will cut it off."
"12903","(12903) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If the fingernail of the Muhrim is broken Let him tell it."
"12904","(12904) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: If the fingernail of a muhrim is broken, he should throw it away."
"12905","(12905) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Maryam, he said: I complained about my nail while I was Muharram, and he hurt me, so I cut him off, so I asked Saeed bin Jubair, and he said: Did he hurt you? So I said: Yes, and he said: So cut it off, my nephew. {Allah desires ease for you and does not desire hardship for you}"
"12906","(12906) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’; In a Muhrim, if his fingernail breaks, he pens it from where it broke, and there is nothing on him, so his pen is not broken. There is blood on it."
"12907","(12907) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: The person in ihram removes his fingernails."
"12908","(12908) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, who said: The person in ihram rubs ulcers, cuts the nails, and cuts the flesh. It removes the eruption, removes the tooth, and treats ulcers."
"12909","(12909) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; In Muharram: he closes the wound, squeezes the ulcer, cuts the nail if it breaks, and mends the break."
"12910","(12910) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is no harm in a person in ihram cutting his skin."
"12911","(12911) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: There is no harm in using the siwak for a person in ihram."
"12912","(12912) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid, who said: They used to like the siwak. For the mahram."
"12913","(12913) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata, who said: There is no harm in using the siwak for a person in ihram."
"12914","(12914) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in a person in ihram staying clean."
"12915","(12915) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr, who said: I said to Ikrimah: Is it permissible for a person in ihram to stay in ihram? He said: Yes, the siwak is pure."
"12916","(12916) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Nafi’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to stay in ihram while he was in ihram."
"12917","(12917) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I asked Muhammad bin Ali, Amir, Ata’, and Tawoos, And Mujahid, and peace, and Al-Qasim, and Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad? They saw no harm in him."
"12918","(12918) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Mujahid, who said: If a person in ihram complains of a tooth, he removes it. And if it breaks, remove it. Mansour said: There is nothing wrong with him."
"12919","(12919) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If a person in ihram complains about his tooth, he can remove it if he wishes."
"12920","(12920) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of someone who informed him, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The person in ihram removes his tooth. And it heals ulcers."
"12921","(12921) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Anbasa, the judge of Rayy, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; About a person in ihram who had his tooth removed and said: There is blood on it."
"12922","(12922) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The tooth is removed, meaning the one in ihram."
"12923","(12923) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Nu’man ibn Malik, who said: I had fun and went to Ibn Abbas, and I said: To him: Indeed, I enjoyed it. He said: {Whatever animal is available}, so I said: What is sheep? He said: Shaah."
"12924","(12924) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man ibn Qais, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: {Whatever animal is found}, Shay."
"12925","(12925) Yahya bin Sulaym al-Taifi told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father (h) and on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: {whatever of the animals is available}, between the cheap and the expensive."
"12926","(12926) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: {Whatever of the guidance is abundant}: Shaya."
"12927","(12927) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: I heard Al-Zuhri, and he was asked about {what is found of guidance}? He said: Ibn Omar used to say: from camels and cows, and Ibn Abbas used to say: from sheep."
"12928","(12928) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: Shaya."
"12929","(12929) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Bura, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: If a man combines Hajj and Umrah, So he had a body burden on him, so it was said to him: Ibn Masoud used to say: A sheep? Ibn Omar said: Fasting is more beloved to me than eating tea."
"12930","(12930) Abdi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim; Aisha and Ibn Umar used to say: The Hadi is from camels and cows."
"12931","(12931) Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Muhammad Ubaid bin Aws, on the authority of Ibn Al-Zubayr, He said: The one with the stomach of a camel or cow."
"12932","(12932) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The camels and cows may become free."
"12933","(12933) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Dulham bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: Shay."
"12934","(12934) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Bakhtari ibn Al-Mukhtar, who said: I heard Ata’ say: Tea."
"12935","(12935) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, who said: I heard Al-Sha’bi say: You divide a sheep in enjoyment"
"12936","(12936) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: “Whatever animal is available” (Shah)."
"12937","(12937) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Bura ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: I came to Ibn Umar and said: I have Hadi, what do you command me to do? He said: A body of cow. Otherwise, fasting for three days and seven days when you return to your family is more beloved to me than tea."
"12938","(12938) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: {Whatever of the animals is easy to find}: Shay."
"12939","(12939) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim; Aisha and Ibn Umar did not see anything except camels and cows, and Ibn Abbas was He says: {Whatever of the Hadith is available} Shaya."
"12940","(12940) Ali and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We were enjoying ourselves with the Messenger of God. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so we slaughter cows for seven people. (Muslim 355. Abu Dawud 2800)"
"12941","(12941) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: It is sufficient for a mutati’ to He shares in blood."
"12942","(12942) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The camel is sufficient. And the cows, about seven, were muttattu’."
"12943","(12943) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The besieged and those who enjoy the world share in common, on the authority of Seven"
"12944","(12944) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’; Indeed, they did not see any harm in the person performing tamattu’ entering into a trap on an island or in a village."
"12945","(12945) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about the people who participate in the sacrifice? She thought about that."
"12946","(12946) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, and Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; Concerning a man who combines Umrah and Hajj and is confined. He said: He sends a sacrificial animal with which it is permissible, then he comes from Qabil with what He was worthy of it."
"12947","(12947) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: He must perform two ‘umrahs. And Hajj"
"12948","(12948) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a man who performed his Umrah and Hajj and was confined, he said: He will be sent with the gift, so when the sacrifice reaches its destination, it is permissible. He said: He is required to perform Hajj and two Umrah, and the ruling said: He is required to perform Hajj and three Umrah."
"12949","(12949) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He is guided."
"12950","(12950) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same."
"12951","(12951) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, and Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He will be sent with a guide and it will be permissible for him to do so."
"12952","(12952) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He has a sacrifice."
"12953","(12953) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus and Ata’, who said: If he combined his Umrah and Hajj and an illness took him away, that is sufficient. There is only one guidance."
"12954","(12954) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he used to say: Whoever the evening overtakes him with manna, It is the second day of the days of Tashreeq, so he should not leave until the next day of the third day."
"12955","(12955) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say that."
"12956","(12956) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, that he used to say: No. He will leave until he is gone tomorrow."
"12957","(12957) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik and Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, that he used to say: He will leave as long as you are not absent. The sun"
"12958","(12958) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, he said: Whoever goes to Mina in the evening on the first day of departure, and intends to depart on that day, should not depart until the next day."
"12959","(12959) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: When the evening reaches you, The second day, so do not leave until tomorrow and the sun has set."
"12960","(12960) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Circumambulating the Kaaba is a prayer. But God Almighty has made sense permissible in it, so whoever speaks should not speak anything but good."
"12961","(12961) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Suleiman, on the authority of a servant of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Sa’id He used to command his sons, when they circumambulated, not to cancel their circumambulation, nor to emigrate, nor to perform a pilgrimage, nor to They will speak to anyone until they complete their circumambulation, if they are able."
"12962","(12962) Abu Saad Muhammad bin Maysar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I circulated behind Ibn Omar and Ibn Abbas, I did not hear either of them speaking during the tawaf."
"12963","(12963) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Circumambulating the Kaaba is a prayer. So speak less about it."
"12964","(12964) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, who said: I walked around with a peacock, but I did not hear him start as a human being. By speaking, unless he speaks to him and he responds."
"12965","(12965) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Al-Furat, who said: Tawoos said: Indeed, I count his spoils as I walk around the Kaaba for a week without anyone speaking to me."
"12966","(12966) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I was circumambulating with Saeed bin Jubayr, and he was speaking to me."
"12967","(12967) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: Shurayh was going around the Kaaba and a man asked him, and he gave him a fatwa."
"12968","(12968) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Sulaiman, who said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr walking around. At home, he speaks to his companions and gives fatwas."
"12969","(12969) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, who said: He was Mujahid, and Sa`id bin Jubayr, Ali bin Abdullah bin Al-Abbas, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan, and Abu Jafar were talking while they were circumambulating the Kaaba. And between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah."
"12970","(12970) Aidh bin Habib told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Tawus, who said: When Abu Musa and Amr bin Al-Aas on behalf of the government. Abu Musa came to perform Umrah, and he and I used to circumambulate the Kaaba when a man approached him. He said: O Abu Musa, is this the temptation that was mentioned? He said: This is nothing but a crop of temptations."
"12971","(12971) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of al-Nadr ibn Ma’bad, who said: I saw Abu Qalabi talking about tawaf."
"12972","(12972) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, who said: I met I asked Abu Masoud while he was circumambulating the Kaaba? So he said to me, then he mentioned a hadith."
"12973","(12973) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Ali, who said: If a person in ihram kisses his wife, then blood must be paid."
"12974","(12974) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata, who said: There is blood on him."
"12975","(12975) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: There is blood on him."
"12976","(12976) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There is blood on him."
"12977","(12977) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There is blood on him."
"12978","(12978) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; If a person in ihram kisses his wife, or makes a sexual wink at his wife, he says: There is blood on him."
"12979","(12979) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he kisses or winks, there is blood on it."
"12980","(12980) Abbad narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ata’: the same as it, and he added or stripped it."
"12981","(12981) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He seeks forgiveness from God."
"12982","(12982) Shababih told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: There is blood on him."
"12983","(12983) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: There is blood on him."
"12984","(12984) Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, on the authority of Hisham Al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Ali Blood"
"12985","(12985) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, who said: There is blood on him."
"12986","(12986) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, who said: Ali Blood"
"12987","(12987) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: If he touches If a person in ihram, or he cheated on his wife, then he must make expiation and give her in charity."
"12988","(12988) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; There is nothing in the touching and touching from behind the garment, and in the touching and touching there is blood."
"12989","(12989) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about a man who had sexual intercourse while in ihram? He said: On his body. I said: What if the greatest water was sent down? He said: Al-Hasan used to say: He is in the same position as the mosques, and he must perform Hajj from the beginning."
"12990","(12990) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ghaylan ibn Jarir, who said: It was me and Hakim ibn al-Duraim. Then a man came to us and said: I put my hand in a place with my wife, but I did not lift it until she was in a state of impurity, so we said: We have no knowledge of it. So they took us to Ali bin Abdullah Al-Bariki, so we came to him and asked him? He said: I have no knowledge of this. While we were like that, we were with Jabir bin Zayd. I said: That is Abu Al-Sha’athi. Come to him and ask him, then return to us and tell us. So he came to him and asked him, then he returned to us, and he will be recognized by human faces. He said: He kept secret from me, so we thought that he had commanded him to make a blood sacrifice."
"12991","(12991) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’; Concerning a man touching his wife and ejaculating, they said: He has a physical obligation, and the Hajj is from someone else."
"12992","(12992) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; In Muharram, he continued until he came down, saying: I think it is obligatory for him to do what is obligatory for the congregations."
"12993","(12993) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no harm in a mirror for a person in ihram."
"12994","(12994) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in him looking at it, or looking away from it. Harm"
"12995","(12995) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He saw nothing wrong with a person in ihram looking in the mirror."
"12996","(12996) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of someone who told him, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (h) and on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata. They said: There is no harm in it."
"12997","(12997) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Amr bin Muslim, on the authority of Tawoos and Ikrimah, who said: No. It is okay for a person in ihram to look in the mirror."
"12998","(12998) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in a person in ihram looking in the mirror."
"12999","(12999) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, he said: Al-Zubayr bin Kharit narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: It was Ibn Abbas does not see any harm in a person in ihram shaving his head or looking in the mirror."
"13000","(13000) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The person in ihram should not look in the mirror, nor should he supplicate for Anyone, even if he wrongs him."
"13001","(13001) Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, that he disliked the ihram to look in the mirror."
"13002","(13002) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn, on the authority of his father, He said: Ibn Abbas and Al-Miswar ibn Makramah disagreed about whether a person in ihram should wash his head. He said: So they sent me to Abu Ayyub. So I came to him while he was bathing between the two horns of the well, and I said: Your nephew, Ibn Abbas, sent me to you, saying: How? Did you see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, washing his head while he was in ihram? So he took some of the water and poured it on his head, then he turned and turned back, then he said: This is how I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He finished washing his head while in ihram, so I returned to them and informed them of what he had said. Al-Miswar said: I will never disagree with you."
"13003","(13003) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Omar said to me: Come Even if I keep you in the water, which of us is more patient? And we are forbidden. (Bukhari 1840 and Abu Dawud 1836)"
"13004","(13004) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Abdullah bin Ma’abad, on the authority of his father, who said: I went out with my maternal aunt. Maymona, so I covered my head with honey or glue while I was in ihram, but it was difficult for me, so I asked her? She said: Dip your head in the water repeatedly."
"13005","(13005) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Muslim Al-Qurayy, who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: I pour water on my head while I Is it forbidden? He said: There is no problem with him, for God Almighty says: (Indeed, God loves those who repent and loves those who purify themselves.)"
"13006","(13006) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no harm for a person in ihram to bathe in water."
"13007","(13007) Abbad narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Taymi, who said: I asked Ibn Umar whether he should take a bath. Muharram? He said: And does that increase anything except Sha``th?"
"13008","(13008) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, he said: There is no harm in washing The person in ihram holds his head and immerses himself in it."
"13009","(13009) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Othman bin Ghayath, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The person in ihram may wash himself with water if he wishes."
"13010","(13010) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm for a person in ihram to bathe with water otherwise. Your honor"
"13011","(13011) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Omar, who said: I poured water on Salim while he was in ihram, but he refused to pour it on me. His head"
"13012","(13012) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm for a person in ihram to bathe without ritual impurity."
"13013","(13013) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: We were in the Gulf of the sea. In Al-Juhfa, we immerse ourselves in it, and Omar looks at us, so what is the shame of that for us, since we are in the state of Ihram?"
"13014","(13014) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hussein, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, permitted the dyed garment for the ihram as long as it does not have any color or deterrent. (Ahmad 1/362, Abu Ali 2572)"
"13015","(13015) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: Aqeel ibn Abi Talib entered ihram in two garments. Two wards. Omar saw him and said: What is this? Ali said to him: No one teaches us the Sunnah."
"13016","(13016) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: There is no harm in the shrine. For the mahram."
"13017","(13017) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father that he He wears flowing clothes, and he is in ihram."
"13018","(13018) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah, He said: The boys were in ihram with Ibn Umar in the city, but he did not forbid them, nor did he disapprove of them."
"13019","(13019) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no problem. Pursued to the ihram."
"13020","(13020) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Muhammad, who said: I saw Salem wearing a flowing garment, meaning, while he was in ihram."
"13021","(13021) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who narrated it, and he said: The person in ihram should not wear a garment. It was touched by roses, but not by saffron. (Bukhari 5794. Ahmad 2/4)"
"13022","(13022) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Aisha, who said: A garment dyed with saffron is disliked. Or one saturated with safflower for men and women, unless it is a garment for washing."
"13023","(13023) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Bura, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that Umar forbade a person in ihram to wear clothing. Dyed with rose and saffron."
"13024","(13024) Jarir told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata, Tawoos, and Mujahid. Indeed, they disliked the inviolability of the ihram."
"13025","(13025) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; He disliked the mahram for the mahram."
"13026","(13026) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated for a man to enter ihram in al-Mu’safar."
